    "https://jobs.charlotte.edu/postings/70377": {
      "title": "Position Information",
      "description": "UNC Charlotte Applicant Site | General Business Counselor Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Frequently Asked Questions Application Process State of NC Salary Chart Campus Security Report Student Employment General Business Counselor Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. The finalist will be subject to a Criminal Background Check and/or a Motor Vehicle Report The Search Committee will not contact references without first verifying permission with the finalist. Please ensure your resume reflects the knowledge, skills, abilities, and experiences to support your answers to the supplemental questions. UNC Charlotte Benefits Information: https://hr.charlotte.edu/benefits/benefits-overview/ Position Information General Information Position Number 008340 Vacancy Open to All Candidates Working Title General Business Counselor Position Designation EHRA Non-Faculty Employment Type Time Limited - Full-time Months per Year 12 Work Schedule 8:00 am – 5:00 pm; Monday – Friday with occasional evening and weekend hours required, as necessary. Hours per week 40 FLSA Status Exempt Division Academic Affairs Department College of Business (Col) Work Location PORTAL Building Salary Range $65,000 Primary Purpose of Department SBTDC’s mission is to support economic development in the State of North Carolina by providing assistance in the start-up, successful operation, and expansion of small businesses and by facilitating technology development and transfer within the state’s small business community. Primary Purpose of Position This position is a senior-level professional position through which the SBTDC’s counseling, training, research, and technical assistance services are provided to small business owners, would-be entrepreneurs, and individuals and firms developing new products, technologies, or markets. The position is expected to provide expert-level business advice and in-depth assistance to a sizable number of clients, both in the Charlotte office and elsewhere throughout an assigned multi-county geographic area. The position also includes group training design/facilitation and marketing/outreach activities. Summary of Position Responsibilities The incumbent is expected to manage a large and varied client portfolio made up of small and medium-sized businesses, as well as pre-venture companies, guiding all business disciplines. Counseling provided is expected to result in economic impact (business starts, revenue generation, sales growth, job creation, etc) and other reportable success stories. The position requires meeting several metrics, including a minimum of 948 hours of counseling activity per year. The incumbent will deliver at least two training events per year (fee-based and/or free), which includes marketing, planning, and/or delivering to target markets in support of the Regional Service Center Annual Work Plan. Duties and Responsibilities Consultation – The Senior Small Business Specialist is independently responsible for managing their client portfolio. This includes a thorough evaluation of complex issue(s) facing clients, and providing consultation based on their expertise. This responsibility includes direct client contact in one-on-one meetings and through telephone and written communications. It also includes the very substantial time which must be committed to adequately research, prepare materials, and recommend courses of action to clients who are counseled. Provide advice and technical assistance relative to complicated, sensitive, and unique problems. Professional Knowledge – Maintain an expert level of knowledge of program policies, procedures, technology, and best practices, specifically as they relate to business growth and management, serving as the local expert in this regard. Analyze and evaluate how issues apply to, or impact, stakeholders, including clients, management or other strategic partners, and then succinctly distill and convey this information. Proactively be aware of changing economic conditions and understand how that might affect the organization or clients, and communicate that information accordingly. Information Analysis / Decision Making – Assess and resolve client issues using financial information, interviews, and other documentation to come up with the data necessary. Review and research multiple sources to support resolution for his/her issue. Must be able to come up with a plan of action to help the client based on one’s own experience and the information available. Applies sound judgment based on experience and training in this analysis and decision making/problem resolution. Communications – Incumbent holds responsibility for proactively promoting the SBTDC throughout the multi-county area served by this center. This includes identifying the most appropriate venues and representing the SBTDC at those meetings and conferences, establishing and growing relationships with potential sources of referrals and with prospective groups of clients. Incumbent also independently develops promotional materials and programs as deemed necessary for this region. Incumbent also represents the program nationally among industry associations as well as peer associations. Program/Project Administration – Much of the work is technically based and requires attention to detail and deadlines. Incumbent must exercise great care and discretion in assisting the SBTDC’s clients based on SBTDC policies and procedures. Absolute confidentiality of client information must be preserved. SBTDC reports must be completed in an accurate and timely manner. National certifications, such as EDFP and other professional development trainings must be kept current in order to effectively administer the program. Leadership – The incumbent in this position is expected to be able to operate with a minimal level of supervision and instruction. He/she is required to assess the needs and benefits of various relationships, independently apply sound judgment and have broad discretion in meeting the goals and responsibilities of this position and the organization as a whole. The incumbent must have the ability to handle multiple assignments, organize work and establish priorities. The incumbent must possess and independently deploy strong skills in problem assessment and resolution and be adept at researching and reviewing lengthy and complex documents. Minimum Education/Experience Bachelor’s degree and one (1) year of experience related to the area of assignment; or an equivalent combination of education and experience. All degrees must be received from appropriately accredited institutions. Preferred Education, Knowledge, Skills and Experience A bachelor’s degree in business administration and a minimum of three years of relevant work experience, or five years of relevant work experience, is preferred. All degrees must be received from appropriately accredited institutions. Prior SBTDC experience is highly preferred. The ideal candidate should have broad knowledge and experience in general business principles and procedures, as well as the ability to communicate, execute, and deploy solutions to overall business issues. Business ownership or business managerial experience is required. Excellent interpersonal and communication skills are essential. The incumbent must have the ability to handle multiple assignments, organize work, and assign priorities with minimal supervision, and must be self-motivated. Public speaking experience is preferred, and the ability to interact with large groups of people is essential. Necessary Certifications/Licenses Preferred Certifications/Licenses Special Notes to Applicants The finalist will be subject to a Criminal Background Check and/or a Motor Vehicle Report The Search Committee will not contact references without first verifying permission with the finalist. Please ensure your resume reflects the knowledge, skills, abilities, and experiences to support your answers to the supplemental questions. UNC Charlotte Benefits Information: https://hr.charlotte.edu/benefits/benefits-overview/ Posting Open Date 09/09/2026 Posting Close Date 10/09/2026 Open Until Filled No Proposed Hire Date 11/01/2026 If time-limited please indicate appointment end date 06/30/2027 Contact Information Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? UNC Charlotte Website HERC Job Board Inside Higher Education Mitratech Circa (formerly known as Local JobNetwork) Another Website Agency Referral Advertisement/Publication Personal Referral Other Where did you learn about this posting? (Open Ended Question) * Do you have at least Bachelor's degree and one year of experience related to area of assignment; or equivalent combination of education and experience? Yes - I have at least a Bachelor's degree and one year of related experience Yes - I have an Associate's degree with at least three of related experience Yes - I have a High School Diploma /GED with at least five years of related experience No * Which of the following best describes your business experience? (Select all that apply.) Business owner/founder CEO/President/General Manager Commercial lender/SBA lender Economic development professional Management consultant/business advisor Corporate functional leader (sales, operations, finance, HR, etc.) Other * Which was the most relevant to the position you are applying for? Please explain. (Open Ended Question) * How many years of direct experience have you had advising, counseling, consulting, lending to, or otherwise supporting small businesses? Briefly describe that experience.\r\n\r\n•\tNone\r\n•\tLess than 2 years\r\n•\t2–5 years\r\n•\t6–10 years\r\n•\tMore than 10 years (Open Ended Question) * This position involves meeting one-on-one with business owners to identify challenges, prioritize opportunities, and connect them with appropriate resources. Describe any professional experience that required similar client-facing advisory work. (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume / Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Contact Information for References Optional Documents 9201 University City Blvd \r\nCharlotte, NC 28223 © 2026 The University of North Carolina at Charlotte. All rights reserved. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.charlotte.edu/postings/70398": {
      "title": "HVAC Technician",
      "description": "UNC Charlotte Applicant Site | HVAC Technician Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Frequently Asked Questions Application Process State of NC Salary Chart Campus Security Report Student Employment HVAC Technician Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. This posting will be used to fill two positions: 010535 & 010527. The finalist will be subject to a Criminal Background Check and/or a Motor Vehicle Report The Search Committee will not contact references without first verifying permission with the finalist . Please ensure your application reflects the knowledge, skills, abilities, and experiences to support your answers to the supplemental questions. Do not write ‘see resume’ on your application when completing the job duties section. UNC Charlotte Benefits Information: https://hr.charlotte.edu/benefits/benefits-overview/ Position Information General Information Vacancy Open to All Candidates Employment Type Permanent - Full-time If time-limited, note appointment end date Hours per week 40 Months per year 12 Position Number 010535 NC Salary Grade Equivalency NC10 Classification Title FM Tech Mechanical Trades Working Title HVAC Technician Salary  Range $42,011 - $57,765 Anticipate Hiring Range $42,011 - $52,514 FLSA Status Non Exempt Division Business Affairs Department Facilities Management (Adm) Work Unit FM HVAC Shop Work Schedule 8:00 am – 4:30 pm; Monday – Friday, with occasional evening and weekend hours required, as necessary, and with an ‘on-call’ designation. This position is designated as ‘mandatory’ and, when contacted to report to work, its incumbent is expected to reach the campus as expeditiously as possible using normal precautions as dictated by the adverse weather conditions. Primary Purpose of Position This is a Facility Maintenance Technician (Mechanical Trades) at the Journey level with a specialty in HVAC . The position is to be fully functioning in a particular trade area. Additionally, this position is expected to be able to perform all general maintenance work at the contributing level. This position may also be allowed to perform/learn another trade discipline either at the contributing or journey level. Tasks may include maintenance, repair, placement, fabrication, installation, alteration, construction, and design of facility components in the assigned zone or core maintenance. Minimum Education/Experience Required Minimum Qualifications: Graduation from high school or equivalent. Experience in the trade(s) areas related to the position’s role may be substituted on a year-for-year basis. Note: Some state job postings state you can qualify by an ‘equivalent combination of education and experience.’ If that language appears above, then you may qualify through EITHER years of education OR years of directly related experience, OR a combination of both. Essential Job Duties Performs comprehensive maintenance, troubleshooting, and repairs on residential and commercial HVAC equipment across a dispersed campus. Manages high-volume service requests, executes preventative maintenance programs, assesses facility damage, and ensures strict adherence to EPA , OSHA , state, and university compliance standards. Other Work Responsibilities Provide skilled general repairs and corrective maintenance for commercial and residential HVAC systems, hot water systems, hydronic equipment, and ice machines. Respond to and resolve approximately 1,000 service calls annually generated through the central work order system across a dispersed campus environment. Troubleshoot system malfunctions, hot/cold complaints, mechanical component failures (such as belt replacements), and software/ DDC control issues. Perform routine preventative maintenance inspections and procedures on commercial and residential systems to ensure efficient operation and extend equipment lifespan. Maintain clean, safe, and optimal physical environments for resident students, guests, and campus facility occupants based on routine inspection findings. Identify, document, and assess damage charges to student or guest accounts when facility or equipment damage is identified during inspections. Maintain departmental responsibility for full compliance with EPA refrigerant regulations, OSHA guidelines, State mechanical codes, and University safety standards across all HVAC activities. Departmental Preferred Experience, Skills, Training/Education EPA 608 Universal Certification Positions may be required to possess and maintain certification, licensure, educational level, and/or experience criteria, as applicable to the tasks being performed, and to follow applicable building codes. Experience with general repairs and corrective maintenance for commercial and residential HVAC systems, hot water systems, hydronic equipment, and ice machines. Necessary Licenses or Certifications Positions may be required to possess and maintain certification, licensure, educational level, and/or experience criteria, as applicable to the tasks being performed, and to follow applicable building codes. Work Location FM Building Posting date 09/10/2026 Closing date 09/23/2026 Proposed Hire Date 09/30/2026 Contact Information 704-687-5173 Special Notes to Applicants This posting will be used to fill two positions: 010535 & 010527. The finalist will be subject to a Criminal Background Check and/or a Motor Vehicle Report The Search Committee will not contact references without first verifying permission with the finalist . Please ensure your application reflects the knowledge, skills, abilities, and experiences to support your answers to the supplemental questions. Do not write ‘see resume’ on your application when completing the job duties section. UNC Charlotte Benefits Information: https://hr.charlotte.edu/benefits/benefits-overview/ Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? UNC Charlotte Website HERC Job Board Inside Higher Education Mitratech Circa (formerly known as Local JobNetwork) Another Website Agency Referral Advertisement/Publication Personal Referral Other Where did you learn about this posting? (Open Ended Question) * Do you have a high school diploma or GED? Experience in the trade(s) areas related to the position’s role may be substituted on a year-for-year basis. Yes, a high school diploma or GED. Yes, experience n the trade(s) areas related to the position’s role that can be substituted for on a year-for-year basis No * Do You have your EPA 608 Certification? Yes No In Process * Do you have experience with general repairs and corrective maintenance for commercial and residential HVAC systems, hot water systems, hydronic equipment, and ice machines? Please explain your experience. (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume / Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents 9201 University City Blvd \r\nCharlotte, NC 28223 © 2026 The University of North Carolina at Charlotte. All rights reserved. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.charlotte.edu/postings/70407": {
      "title": "Events Coordinator",
      "description": "UNC Charlotte Applicant Site | Events Coordinator Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Frequently Asked Questions Application Process State of NC Salary Chart Campus Security Report Student Employment Events Coordinator Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. The finalist will be subject to a Criminal Background Check and/or a Motor Vehicle Report The Search Committee will not contact references without first verifying permission with the finalist. Please ensure your application reflects the knowledge, skills, abilities, and experiences to support your answers to the supplemental questions. Do not write ‘see resume’ on your application when completing the job duties section. UNC Charlotte Benefits Information: https://hr.charlotte.edu/benefits/benefits-overview/ Position Information General Information Vacancy Open to All Candidates Employment Type Permanent - Full-time If time-limited, note appointment end date Hours per week 40 Months per year 12 Position Number 009040 NC Salary Grade Equivalency NC07 Classification Title Student Services Specialist - Journey Working Title Events Coordinator Salary  Range $39,058 - $53,705 Anticipate Hiring Range $39,058 - $48,823 FLSA Status Non Exempt Division Athletics Department Athletics Venues (Adm) Work Unit Student Activity Ctr and Venue Mgmt Work Schedule 8:00 am – 5:00 pm; Monday – Friday with flexible evening and weekend hours required in conjunction with event schedules. Primary Purpose of Position This position serves as an Event Coordinator, responsible for coordinating event and meeting logistics, as well as providing invoicing and tracking of event satisfaction. Serves as Event Manager for designated events within Venue Management spaces. Assists in the hiring, training, and supervision of student event staff. Also supervises contracted event staff and medical personnel when deemed necessary. Minimum Education/Experience Required Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree; or equivalent combination of education and experience. All degrees must be received from appropriately accredited institutions. Note: Some state job postings state you can qualify by an ‘equivalent combination of education and experience.’ If that language appears above, then you may qualify through EITHER years of education OR years of directly related experience, OR a combination of both. Essential Job Duties Serves as Event Manager for designated events throughout the facility. Acts as the on-site liaison for Salon space, meeting with clients to anticipate issues and assisting clients in developing a sound, successful event plan. Role as onsite liaison for Salons includes working with clients throughout the duration of the event process, including pre-event preparation, event, and post-event evaluation. Prepares and distributes 25live report(s) and event calendar(s) on a weekly basis. Gathers and disseminates all pertinent event-related information to various areas in the department, and where applicable, to the university community. Coordinates appropriate staffing needs based on event needs, including both university and contracted staffing. Oversees the collection of post-event surveys to benchmark customer satisfaction. Develops and maintains strong relationships with both internal and external customers while developing work relations with key partners across campus. Provides excellent customer service to clients, patrons, visitors, and fellow staff. Ensures event compliance with all safety, fire, and security regulations as well as a working knowledge of ADA requirements. Proactively works to ensure a safe environment is provided for patrons, clients, and staff. Conducts and participates in bi-weekly Event Meetings to engage fellow staff to identify challenges and areas for improvement. Other Work Responsibilities Develop and maintain strong working relationships with University departments involved in event operations, including Conference Services, University Recreation, Facilities Management, Parking, Police, and Catering. Departmental Preferred Experience, Skills, Training/Education Experience in recreation, sport management, higher education, large conferences, athletics, or event planning and execution. Experience in scheduling, training, and managing student staff. Experience with event-specific diagramming and scheduling software. Strong background in customer service, safety, and security. Experience and/or working knowledge of crowd management best practices, ADA requirements, and fire code regulations Necessary Licenses or Certifications Work Location Student Activity Center & Other Athletic Facilities Posting date 09/10/2026 Closing date 09/17/2026 Proposed Hire Date 10/12/2026 Contact Information Special Notes to Applicants The finalist will be subject to a Criminal Background Check and/or a Motor Vehicle Report The Search Committee will not contact references without first verifying permission with the finalist. Please ensure your application reflects the knowledge, skills, abilities, and experiences to support your answers to the supplemental questions. Do not write ‘see resume’ on your application when completing the job duties section. UNC Charlotte Benefits Information: https://hr.charlotte.edu/benefits/benefits-overview/ Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? UNC Charlotte Website HERC Job Board Inside Higher Education Mitratech Circa (formerly known as Local JobNetwork) Another Website Agency Referral Advertisement/Publication Personal Referral Other Where did you learn about this posting? (Open Ended Question) * Do you have a Bachelor's degree, or an equivalent combination of training and experience? Yes - Bachelor's degree or Higher Yes - Associate's degree with at least two years relative experience to the position Yes - High School/GED with at least four years relative experience to the position No * Do you have experience in recreation, sport management, higher education, large conferences, athletics, or event planning and execution? Please explain your experience. (Open Ended Question) * Please describe your experience hiring and supervising student employees. (Open Ended Question) * Do you have experience with event-specific diagramming and scheduling software? Please explain your experience. (Open Ended Question) * Please describe your experience and knowledge in ADA, building codes, and crowd management. (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume / Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Contact Information for References Optional Documents 9201 University City Blvd \r\nCharlotte, NC 28223 © 2026 The University of North Carolina at Charlotte. All rights reserved. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
