    "https://jobs.charlotte.edu/postings/70408": {
      "title": "Guest Services Coordinator",
      "description": "UNC Charlotte Applicant Site | Guest Services Coordinator Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Frequently Asked Questions Application Process State of NC Salary Chart Campus Security Report Student Employment Guest Services Coordinator Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. The finalist will be subject to a Criminal Background Check and/or a Motor Vehicle Report The Search Committee will not contact references without first verifying permission with the finalist. Please ensure your application reflects the knowledge, skills, abilities, and experiences to support your answers to the supplemental questions. Do not write ‘see resume’ on your application when completing the job duties section. UNC Charlotte Benefits Information: https://hr.charlotte.edu/benefits/benefits-overview/ Position Information General Information Vacancy Open to All Candidates Employment Type Permanent - Full-time If time-limited, note appointment end date Hours per week 40 Months per year 12 Position Number 012933 NC Salary Grade Equivalency NC07 Classification Title Student Services Specialist - Journey Working Title Guest Services Coordinator Salary  Range $39,058 - $53,705 Anticipate Hiring Range $39,058 - $48,823 FLSA Status Non Exempt Division Athletics Department Athletics Venues (Adm) Work Unit Student Activity Ctr and Venue Mgmt Work Schedule 10:00 am – 7:00 pm; Monday – Friday, with a flexible schedule to include evening, weekend, and holiday hours as necessary in conjunction with event schedules. Mandatory Position Primary Purpose of Position This position serves as the Guest Services Coordinator for the Student Activity Center and Venue Management, with responsibility for serving as a primary point of contact with guests and student staff to high quality experiences for all patrons. Additionally, this position provides oversight and supervision of 40+ student employees to ensure superior customer service, access, and daily facilities operations. Serves as the administrator on duty during (non-event) evening hours. Minimum Education/Experience Required Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree; or equivalent combination of education and experience. All degrees must be received from appropriately accredited institutions. Note: Some state job postings state you can qualify by an ‘equivalent combination of education and experience.’ If that language appears above, then you may qualify through EITHER years of education OR years of directly related experience, OR a combination of both. Essential Job Duties The Guest Services Manager is responsible for overseeing the daily function of the facility Hire, train, supervise, and evaluate 40+ student staff. Oversee facility use and access, including providing evening and weekend supervision as needed. Complete staff scheduling to ensure appropriate coverage for all operating hours of the Student Activity Center and Student Event Staff coverage. Provide event support as needed. Ensure safety and security of guests, staff, and facilities. Provide excellent customer service. Serve as Administrator on Duty during (non-event) evening hours. Other Work Responsibilities Develop and maintain strong working relationships with University departments, including University Recreation, Athletics, Conference Services, Concessions, and other departments Engage in the success of all team members. Complete monthly payroll for student employees, tracking payroll expenses to ensure annual expenditures are consistent with the approved budget, and report to the Assistant Director of Events/Halton Arena. Provide feedback for facility and risk management policies for SAC and Athletic Venues. Ensure staff has been adequately trained on Emergency Response and Evacuation Plans for both daily and event operations. Departmental Preferred Experience, Skills, Training/Education Experience in the area of Student Affairs, event management, or other related fields with a strong background in customer service, safety, and the student environment. Experience with the hiring, training, and management of student staff and interns, requiring patience and adaptability to frequent changes in student staff scheduling. Experience/knowledge in ADA , building codes, and/or crowd management Strong interpersonal skills and the ability to work with, supervise, and lead a varied population. Necessary Licenses or Certifications Work Location Student Activity Center & Other Athletic Facilities Posting date 09/10/2026 Closing date 09/17/2026 Proposed Hire Date 10/22/2026 Contact Information Special Notes to Applicants The finalist will be subject to a Criminal Background Check and/or a Motor Vehicle Report The Search Committee will not contact references without first verifying permission with the finalist. Please ensure your application reflects the knowledge, skills, abilities, and experiences to support your answers to the supplemental questions. Do not write ‘see resume’ on your application when completing the job duties section. UNC Charlotte Benefits Information: https://hr.charlotte.edu/benefits/benefits-overview/ Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? UNC Charlotte Website HERC Job Board Inside Higher Education Mitratech Circa (formerly known as Local JobNetwork) Another Website Agency Referral Advertisement/Publication Personal Referral Other Where did you learn about this posting? (Open Ended Question) * Do you have a Bachelor's Degree or an equivalent combination of training and experience? No Yes- I have Bachelor's Degree or Higher Yes - I have an Associate's Degree and at least two (2) years of experience related to the position Yes- I have a High School Diploma/GED and at least four (4) years of experience related to the position * Do you have experience in the area of Student Affairs, event management, or other related fields with a strong background in customer service, safety, and the student environment? Please explain your experience. (Open Ended Question) * Do you have experience with the hiring, training, and management of student staff and interns, requiring patience and adaptability to frequent changes in student staff scheduling? Please explain your experience. (Open Ended Question) * Please describe your experience and knowledge in ADA, building codes, and crowd management. (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume / Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Contact Information for References Optional Documents 9201 University City Blvd \r\nCharlotte, NC 28223 © 2026 The University of North Carolina at Charlotte. All rights reserved. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
