    "https://jobs.charlotte.edu/postings/70510": {
      "title": "Position Information",
      "description": "UNC Charlotte Applicant Site | Facility Planner II - (Project Manager) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Frequently Asked Questions Application Process State of NC Salary Chart Campus Security Report Student Employment Facility Planner II - (Project Manager) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. The finalist will be subject to a Criminal Background Check and/or a Motor Vehicle Report The Search Committee will not contact references without first verifying permission with the finalist . Please ensure your resume reflects the knowledge, skills, abilities, and experiences to support your answers to the supplemental questions. UNC Charlotte Benefits Information: https://hr.charlotte.edu/benefits/benefits-overview/ Position Information General Information Position Number 009484 Vacancy Open to All Candidates Working Title Facility Planner II - (Project Manager) Position Designation EHRA Non-Faculty Employment Type Permanent - Full-time Months per Year 12 Work Schedule Monday – Friday, 8:00 am – 5:00 pm This position is also eligible for 1 day of telework per week with supervisor permission. Hours per week 40 FLSA Status Exempt Division Business Affairs Department Facilities Management (Adm) Work Location FM/PPS Salary Range $78,246 - $80,600 Primary Purpose of Department The Planning, Design, and Construction department manages the design and planning of informal and capital projects for the university community. Primary Purpose of Position The primary responsibility of the Facility Planner II (Project Manager) is to manage the planning, programming, design, and construction administration of university projects. Projects will range in scope and dollar value, to coincide with both informal and capital projects. The incumbent will manage projects from the planning phase, carrying the project through the construction phase, and finally to project close-out. Summary of Position Responsibilities Display and apply thorough expertise and understanding of concepts, practices, and theories used in the field of project management. Lead facility planning and project management for assigned campus projects. Oversee design and construction of a variety of University projects to include planning, design (all phases), bidding and contracting, budgets, schedules, etc., from advanced planning through project closeout. Manage implementation of projects and plans according to codes and regulations. Provide consultation and technical assistance as required for projects. Review codes to ensure compliance related to ADA , state construction statutes, the NC State Building Code, fire, and other oversight codes. Responsible for development and posting of all RFP’s and RFQ’s for assigned projects. Display and apply thoroughly developed knowledge of business and management principles involved in strategic planning, problem solving, budget analysis, and coordination of people and resources. Meet with campus stakeholders to develop creative, interactive, budget-appropriate proposals. Conduct project meetings, as required. Guide, direct, and coordinate design consultants as assigned. Process all project transactions such as contractor and designer pay applications, construction contract change orders, and designer contract amendments. Perform other duties as assigned and/or delegated to support all PDC operations. Minimum Education/Experience Bachelor’s degree in institutional planning, public administration, engineering, architecture, business administration, economics, industrial technology, or a related discipline and two years of facility planning or project management experience; or an equivalent combination of training and experience. All degrees must be received from appropriately accredited institutions. Preferred Education, Knowledge, Skills and Experience Experience in shepherding a project from RFP / RFQ to project completion Experience with projects with FFE and/or an interior design scope Experience in managing multiple projects of various sizes and scopes simultaneously Experience with project billing and budget management Familiarity with North Carolina State construction process Necessary Certifications/Licenses Preferred Certifications/Licenses Special Notes to Applicants The finalist will be subject to a Criminal Background Check and/or a Motor Vehicle Report The Search Committee will not contact references without first verifying permission with the finalist . Please ensure your resume reflects the knowledge, skills, abilities, and experiences to support your answers to the supplemental questions. UNC Charlotte Benefits Information: https://hr.charlotte.edu/benefits/benefits-overview/ Posting Open Date 09/15/2026 Posting Close Date 09/21/2026 Open Until Filled No Proposed Hire Date 10/12/2026 If time-limited please indicate appointment end date Contact Information Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? UNC Charlotte Website HERC Job Board Inside Higher Education Mitratech Circa (formerly known as Local JobNetwork) Another Website Agency Referral Advertisement/Publication Personal Referral Other Where did you learn about this posting? (Open Ended Question) * Do you have a bachelor's degree in institutional planning, public administration, engineering, architecture, business administration, economics, industrial technology or a related discipline and two years of facility planning or project management experience; or equivalent combination of training and experience? Yes, I have a Bachelor’s degree in institutional planning, public administration, engineering, architecture, business administration, economics, industrial technology or a related discipline and two (2) years of facility planning or project management exp Yes, I have an Associates degree degree in institutional planning, public administration, engineering, architecture, business administration, economics, industrial technology or a related discipline and two (2) years of facility planning or project manage Yes, I have a high school diploma/GED and six (6) years of the equivalent combination of training and experience No, I do not Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume / Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Optional Documents Contact Information for References 9201 University City Blvd \r\nCharlotte, NC 28223 © 2026 The University of North Carolina at Charlotte. All rights reserved. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.charlotte.edu/postings/70519": {
      "title": "Position Information",
      "description": "UNC Charlotte Applicant Site | General Business Counselor Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Frequently Asked Questions Application Process State of NC Salary Chart Campus Security Report Student Employment General Business Counselor Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. The finalist will be subject to a Criminal Background Check and/or a Motor Vehicle Report The Search Committee will not contact references without first verifying permission with the finalist. Please ensure your resume reflects the knowledge, skills, abilities, and experiences to support your answers to the supplemental questions. UNC Charlotte Benefits Information: https://hr.charlotte.edu/benefits/benefits-overview/ Position Information General Information Position Number 008340 Vacancy Open to All Candidates Working Title General Business Counselor Position Designation EHRA Non-Faculty Employment Type Time Limited - Full-time Months per Year 12 Work Schedule 8:00 am – 5:00 pm; Monday – Friday with occasional evening and weekend hours required, as necessary. Hours per week 40 FLSA Status Exempt Division Academic Affairs Department College of Business (Col) Work Location PORTAL Building Salary Range $65,000 Primary Purpose of Department SBTDC’s mission is to support economic development in the State of North Carolina by providing assistance in the start-up, successful operation, and expansion of small businesses and by facilitating technology development and transfer within the state’s small business community. Primary Purpose of Position This position is a senior-level professional position through which the SBTDC’s counseling, training, research, and technical assistance services are provided to small business owners, would-be entrepreneurs, and individuals and firms developing new products, technologies, or markets. The position is expected to provide expert-level business advice and in-depth assistance to a sizable number of clients, both in the Charlotte office and elsewhere throughout an assigned multi-county geographic area. The position also includes group training design/facilitation and marketing/outreach activities. Summary of Position Responsibilities The incumbent is expected to manage a large and varied client portfolio made up of small and medium-sized businesses, as well as pre-venture companies, guiding all business disciplines. Counseling provided is expected to result in economic impact (business starts, revenue generation, sales growth, job creation, etc) and other reportable success stories. The position requires meeting several metrics, including a minimum of 948 hours of counseling activity per year. The incumbent will deliver at least two training events per year (fee-based and/or free), which includes marketing, planning, and/or delivering to target markets in support of the Regional Service Center Annual Work Plan. Duties and Responsibilities Consultation – The Senior Small Business Specialist is independently responsible for managing their client portfolio. This includes a thorough evaluation of complex issue(s) facing clients, and providing consultation based on their expertise. This responsibility includes direct client contact in one-on-one meetings and through telephone and written communications. It also includes the very substantial time which must be committed to adequately research, prepare materials, and recommend courses of action to clients who are counseled. Provide advice and technical assistance relative to complicated, sensitive, and unique problems. Professional Knowledge – Maintain an expert level of knowledge of program policies, procedures, technology, and best practices, specifically as they relate to business growth and management, serving as the local expert in this regard. Analyze and evaluate how issues apply to, or impact, stakeholders, including clients, management or other strategic partners, and then succinctly distill and convey this information. Proactively be aware of changing economic conditions and understand how that might affect the organization or clients, and communicate that information accordingly. Information Analysis / Decision Making – Assess and resolve client issues using financial information, interviews, and other documentation to come up with the data necessary. Review and research multiple sources to support resolution for his/her issue. Must be able to come up with a plan of action to help the client based on one’s own experience and the information available. Applies sound judgment based on experience and training in this analysis and decision making/problem resolution. Communications – Incumbent holds responsibility for proactively promoting the SBTDC throughout the multi-county area served by this center. This includes identifying the most appropriate venues and representing the SBTDC at those meetings and conferences, establishing and growing relationships with potential sources of referrals and with prospective groups of clients. Incumbent also independently develops promotional materials and programs as deemed necessary for this region. Incumbent also represents the program nationally among industry associations as well as peer associations. Program/Project Administration – Much of the work is technically based and requires attention to detail and deadlines. Incumbent must exercise great care and discretion in assisting the SBTDC’s clients based on SBTDC policies and procedures. Absolute confidentiality of client information must be preserved. SBTDC reports must be completed in an accurate and timely manner. National certifications, such as EDFP and other professional development trainings must be kept current in order to effectively administer the program. Leadership – The incumbent in this position is expected to be able to operate with a minimal level of supervision and instruction. He/she is required to assess the needs and benefits of various relationships, independently apply sound judgment and have broad discretion in meeting the goals and responsibilities of this position and the organization as a whole. The incumbent must have the ability to handle multiple assignments, organize work and establish priorities. The incumbent must possess and independently deploy strong skills in problem assessment and resolution and be adept at researching and reviewing lengthy and complex documents. Minimum Education/Experience Bachelor’s degree and one (1) year of experience related to the area of assignment; or an equivalent combination of education and experience. All degrees must be received from appropriately accredited institutions. Preferred Education, Knowledge, Skills and Experience A bachelor’s degree in business administration and a minimum of three years of relevant work experience, or five years of relevant work experience, is preferred. All degrees must be received from appropriately accredited institutions. Prior SBTDC experience is highly preferred. The ideal candidate should have broad knowledge and experience in general business principles and procedures, as well as the ability to communicate, execute, and deploy solutions to overall business issues. Business ownership or business managerial experience is required. Excellent interpersonal and communication skills are essential. The incumbent must have the ability to handle multiple assignments, organize work, and assign priorities with minimal supervision, and must be self-motivated. Public speaking experience is preferred, and the ability to interact with large groups of people is essential. Necessary Certifications/Licenses Preferred Certifications/Licenses Special Notes to Applicants The finalist will be subject to a Criminal Background Check and/or a Motor Vehicle Report The Search Committee will not contact references without first verifying permission with the finalist. Please ensure your resume reflects the knowledge, skills, abilities, and experiences to support your answers to the supplemental questions. UNC Charlotte Benefits Information: https://hr.charlotte.edu/benefits/benefits-overview/ Posting Open Date 09/09/2026 Posting Close Date 10/09/2026 Open Until Filled No Proposed Hire Date 11/01/2026 If time-limited please indicate appointment end date 06/30/2027 Contact Information Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? UNC Charlotte Website HERC Job Board Inside Higher Education Mitratech Circa (formerly known as Local JobNetwork) Another Website Agency Referral Advertisement/Publication Personal Referral Other Where did you learn about this posting? (Open Ended Question) * Do you have a Bachelor's degree and one (1) year of experience related to area of assignment; or equivalent combination of education and experience? Yes - I have at least a Bachelor's degree and one year of related experience Yes - I have an Associate's degree with at least three of related experience Yes - I have a High School Diploma /GED with at least five years of related experience No * Which of the following best describes your business experience? (Select all that apply.) Business owner/founder CEO/President/General Manager Commercial lender/SBA lender Economic development professional Management consultant/business advisor Corporate functional leader (sales, operations, finance, HR, etc.) Other * Which was the most relevant to the position you are applying for? Please explain. (Open Ended Question) * How many years of direct experience have you had advising, counseling, consulting, lending to, or otherwise supporting small businesses? Briefly describe that experience.\r\n\r\n•\tNone\r\n•\tLess than 2 years\r\n•\t2–5 years\r\n•\t6–10 years\r\n•\tMore than 10 years (Open Ended Question) * This position involves meeting one-on-one with business owners to identify challenges, prioritize opportunities, and connect them with appropriate resources. Describe any professional experience that required similar client-facing advisory work. (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume / Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Contact Information for References Optional Documents 9201 University City Blvd \r\nCharlotte, NC 28223 © 2026 The University of North Carolina at Charlotte. All rights reserved. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
