    "https://jobs.charlotte.edu/postings/70498": {
      "title": "HVAC Technician",
      "description": "UNC Charlotte Applicant Site | HVAC Technician Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Frequently Asked Questions Application Process State of NC Salary Chart Campus Security Report Student Employment HVAC Technician Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. This posting will be used to fill two positions: 010535 & 010527. The finalist will be subject to a Criminal Background Check and/or a Motor Vehicle Report The Search Committee will not contact references without first verifying permission with the finalist . Please ensure your application reflects the knowledge, skills, abilities, and experiences to support your answers to the supplemental questions. Do not write ‘see resume’ on your application when completing the job duties section. UNC Charlotte Benefits Information: https://hr.charlotte.edu/benefits/benefits-overview/ Position Information General Information Vacancy Open to All Candidates Employment Type Permanent - Full-time If time-limited, note appointment end date Hours per week 40 Months per year 12 Position Number 010535 NC Salary Grade Equivalency NC10 Classification Title FM Tech Mechanical Trades Working Title HVAC Technician Salary  Range $42,011 - $57,765 Anticipate Hiring Range $42,011 - $52,514 FLSA Status Non Exempt Division Business Affairs Department Facilities Management (Adm) Work Unit FM HVAC Shop Work Schedule 8:00 am – 4:30 pm; Monday – Friday, with occasional evening and weekend hours required, as necessary, and with an ‘on-call’ designation. This position is designated as ‘mandatory’ and, when contacted to report to work, its incumbent is expected to reach the campus as expeditiously as possible using normal precautions as dictated by the adverse weather conditions. Primary Purpose of Position This is a Facility Maintenance Technician (Mechanical Trades) at the Journey level with a specialty in HVAC . The position is to be fully functioning in a particular trade area. Additionally, this position is expected to be able to perform all general maintenance work at the contributing level. This position may also be allowed to perform/learn another trade discipline either at the contributing or journey level. Tasks may include maintenance, repair, placement, fabrication, installation, alteration, construction, and design of facility components in the assigned zone or core maintenance. Minimum Education/Experience Required Minimum Qualifications: Graduation from high school or equivalent. Experience in the trade(s) areas related to the position’s role may be substituted on a year-for-year basis. Note: Some state job postings state you can qualify by an ‘equivalent combination of education and experience.’ If that language appears above, then you may qualify through EITHER years of education OR years of directly related experience, OR a combination of both. Essential Job Duties Performs comprehensive maintenance, troubleshooting, and repairs on residential and commercial HVAC equipment across a dispersed campus. Manages high-volume service requests, executes preventative maintenance programs, assesses facility damage, and ensures strict adherence to EPA , OSHA , state, and university compliance standards. Other Work Responsibilities Provide skilled general repairs and corrective maintenance for commercial and residential HVAC systems, hot water systems, hydronic equipment, and ice machines. Respond to and resolve approximately 1,000 service calls annually generated through the central work order system across a dispersed campus environment. Troubleshoot system malfunctions, hot/cold complaints, mechanical component failures (such as belt replacements), and software/ DDC control issues. Perform routine preventative maintenance inspections and procedures on commercial and residential systems to ensure efficient operation and extend equipment lifespan. Maintain clean, safe, and optimal physical environments for resident students, guests, and campus facility occupants based on routine inspection findings. Identify, document, and assess damage charges to student or guest accounts when facility or equipment damage is identified during inspections. Maintain departmental responsibility for full compliance with EPA refrigerant regulations, OSHA guidelines, State mechanical codes, and University safety standards across all HVAC activities. Departmental Preferred Experience, Skills, Training/Education EPA 608 Universal Certification Positions may be required to possess and maintain certification, licensure, educational level, and/or experience criteria, as applicable to the tasks being performed, and to follow applicable building codes. Experience with general repairs and corrective maintenance for commercial and residential HVAC systems, hot water systems, hydronic equipment, and ice machines. Necessary Licenses or Certifications Positions may be required to possess and maintain certification, licensure, educational level, and/or experience criteria, as applicable to the tasks being performed, and to follow applicable building codes. Work Location FM Building Posting date 09/10/2026 Closing date 09/23/2026 Proposed Hire Date 09/30/2026 Contact Information 704-687-5173 Special Notes to Applicants This posting will be used to fill two positions: 010535 & 010527. The finalist will be subject to a Criminal Background Check and/or a Motor Vehicle Report The Search Committee will not contact references without first verifying permission with the finalist . Please ensure your application reflects the knowledge, skills, abilities, and experiences to support your answers to the supplemental questions. Do not write ‘see resume’ on your application when completing the job duties section. UNC Charlotte Benefits Information: https://hr.charlotte.edu/benefits/benefits-overview/ Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? UNC Charlotte Website HERC Job Board Inside Higher Education Mitratech Circa (formerly known as Local JobNetwork) Another Website Agency Referral Advertisement/Publication Personal Referral Other Where did you learn about this posting? (Open Ended Question) * Do you have a high school diploma or GED? Experience in the trade(s) areas related to the position’s role may be substituted on a year-for-year basis. Yes, a high school diploma or GED. Yes, experience n the trade(s) areas related to the position’s role that can be substituted for on a year-for-year basis No * Do You have your EPA 608 Certification? Yes No In Process * Do you have experience with general repairs and corrective maintenance for commercial and residential HVAC systems, hot water systems, hydronic equipment, and ice machines? Please explain your experience. (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume / Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents 9201 University City Blvd \r\nCharlotte, NC 28223 © 2026 The University of North Carolina at Charlotte. All rights reserved. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.charlotte.edu/postings/70507": {
      "title": "Associate Director for Employer Development",
      "description": "UNC Charlotte Applicant Site | Associate Director for Employer Development Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Frequently Asked Questions Application Process State of NC Salary Chart Campus Security Report Student Employment Associate Director for Employer Development Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. The finalist will be subject to a Criminal Background Check and/or a Motor Vehicle Report The Search Committee will not contact references without first verifying permission with the finalist . Please ensure your resume reflects the knowledge, skills, abilities, and experiences to support your answers to the supplemental questions. UNC Charlotte Benefits Information: https://hr.charlotte.edu/benefits/benefits-overview/ Position Information General Information Position Number 000788 Vacancy Open to All Candidates Working Title Associate Director for Employer Development Position Designation EHRA Non-Faculty Employment Type Permanent - Full-time Months per Year 12 Work Schedule Monday -Friday, 8:00 am to 5:00 pm, some weekends and evenings as required. Hours per week 40 FLSA Status Exempt Division Academic Affairs Department University College (Adm) Work Location Career Center Salary Range $73,000 - $79,434 Primary Purpose of Department The Career Center is committed to providing comprehensive, innovative services and resources for students, alumni, and employers that prepare UNC Charlotte graduates for the competitive global market. Through a focus on early, continuous career and professional preparation, we bridge academic knowledge and professional development. We seek campus and employer partnerships to connect students with meaningful, real-world experiences, leading to success for both UNC Charlotte alumni and the greater Charlotte community. Primary Purpose of Position The Associate Director for Employer Development strategically manages and develops employer relationships across all industries, ensuring every campus constituent who interfaces with employers — Colleges, Advancement, Alumni Relations, and other institutional partners — moves in a coordinated, unified direction. This position leads the Employer Development team, directly supervising staff responsible for industry-specific employer relationships, part-time and event-based employer engagement, and the strategic growth of new employer partnerships. The Associate Director sets employer development direction and defines employer engagement metrics, owns employer engagement reporting for campus leadership, and serves as the primary point of contact for major employer initiatives arising from across campus — including the Corporate Relations Council, University Advancement, and University Leadership. This position works in close, ongoing coordination with the Associate Director for Experiential Learning — as a peer partner, not a supervisory relationship — to ensure a unified, one-university approach to employer and internship-related opportunities. This position supervises full-time staff and carries budgetary responsibility for the Employer Development team. Summary of Position Responsibilities Strategic Leadership of Employer Development Sets and manages the strategic direction for employer engagement, ensuring it addresses University College and UNC Charlotte’s broader strategic initiatives and remains flexible and proactive as workplace and workforce trends change. Provides leadership and supervision for the Employer Development team, including staff managing Top 50 Employer relationships, the Employer Partners Program, industry-specific relationship development, and part-time/event-based employer engagement. Leads annual strategic planning, goal-setting, and performance management for the Employer Development team; proposes annual employer outreach and relationship targets for all center staff who manage employer relationships, which are finalized in agreement with the Associate Dean each year and factored into performance review. Manages strategy development, staffing, and budget for the Employer Development team, with full decision-making authority within the team’s own budget. Maintains a monthly coordination cadence with the Associate Director for Experiential Learning to align dashboards, targets, and strategy across both teams, and to resolve cross-cutting employer or opportunity needs. Researches and stays informed on hiring practices, employment trends, and labor-market issues; shares lessons learned across the Employer Development team and broader office staff. Employer Relationship & Metrics Management Sets annual employer outreach targets for those who are responsible for employer development and drives new relationship development; success is measured by meeting or exceeding target lists, with at least two documented touchpoints per target relationship. Owns the health and maintenance of existing major employer relationships, ensuring semesterly contact — at minimum, a check-in — with every relationship at “High” or “Medium-High” status in Forge. Builds and maintains a near-live, trackable dashboard for university leadership to view relationship health and progress against targets; solely responsible for building and maintaining this system. Manages the employer relationship management system (Forge) used across the team, ensuring employer notes, contact history, and relationship status remain accurate and current. Routes new and incoming employer contacts to the appropriate team member based on industry focus and relationship ownership; handles overflow and as-needed employer relationships directly. Advises existing employers on marketing strategies, appropriateness of employer expectations, recruiting processes, job descriptions, salary negotiations, and related employer-facing guidance. Major Employer Initiatives & Campus Partnerships Serves as the primary point of contact for the Corporate Relations Council, fielding tasks and information needs arising from Council meetings, Chancellor- or Provost-sponsored initiatives, new sub-industries to pursue, and cross-campus collaboration or strategic communications needs. Serves as the default point of contact for campus partner inquiries not specifically tied to Experiential Learning, including Advancement and Alumni Relations. Ensures career educational opportunities (Panels in Residence, Meet Ups, and similar events) are filled with employers and alumni from the relevant fields. Represents the Employer Development team on university and community committees, workgroups, and events related to employer partnerships and workforce development, including Chamber meetings, Workforce Development meetings, and evening networking events. Manages high-visibility or strategic employer relationships, including those tied to corporate sponsorships or major donors, in coordination with Advancement and other campus stakeholders; escalates unusual or sensitive situations — such as legal/contract terms or major donor relationships — to the Associate Dean. Publishes the semesterly Industry Report — bundling industry engagement levels, new employer development against targets, and the Top 50 Companies Report (the latter developed with input from the Associate Director for Experiential Learning) — for internal leadership and key campus constituents. All reports route to the Associate Dean for final review before publishing. Employer Development Team Leadership Directly supervises staff managing Top 50 Employer relationships, the Employer Partners Program, the JLD Program, part-time job development, and industry-specific relationship management. Maintains direct relationship-building responsibility for at least one industry focus area, modeling the relationship-management standard expected across the team. Shares responsibility with the Experiential Learning team for ensuring all career education opportunities are staffed by relevant employers and alumni. Specialized Projects/Other Responsibilities Represents the Employer Development team in university, community, and networking events, employer site visits, and on-campus hosting for employer cultivation purposes. Develops and maintains employer-facing guidelines for recruitment. Makes independent decisions on employer partnerships at the Career Center level; anything representing the university as a whole is elevated to the Associate Dean. Assists office leadership in preparing and managing the departmental budget. Other duties as necessary to support office function and operations. Minimum Education/Experience Master’s degree in higher education administration, business, human resources, or a related field with commensurate experience. Progressive professional experience in employer relations, career services, business development, account/relationship management, or a comparable relationship-driven field. Experience directly supervising and developing staff, including performance management and goal-setting. Preferred Education, Knowledge, Skills and Experience Experience operating with significant decision-making autonomy — able to exercise sound judgment on partnership and relationship decisions without needing frequent sign-off, while knowing when an issue genuinely warrants escalation. Comfort with CRM or relationship-tracking systems and building reporting dashboards; this role is expected to build and maintain its own tracking. Experience in a role requiring peer-level cross-functional coordination — working alongside another leader with a related but distinct mandate, without a direct reporting relationship between them. Familiarity working with or presenting to senior institutional leadership (e.g., cabinet-level administrators, boards, or executive councils). Business development instincts — comfortable proactively pursuing new relationships against a target list, not just maintaining existing ones. Experience operating across multiple industries or client verticals simultaneously, given the breadth of employer sectors this role touches. Demonstrated experience owning a major initiative with clearly defined metrics and milestones — not just contributing to one, but having accountability for setting the targets, tracking progress, and reporting outcomes to leadership. Proven ability to set goals, track progress against them, and move a team or group of stakeholders toward measurable results. Necessary Certifications/Licenses Preferred Certifications/Licenses Special Notes to Applicants The finalist will be subject to a Criminal Background Check and/or a Motor Vehicle Report The Search Committee will not contact references without first verifying permission with the finalist . Please ensure your resume reflects the knowledge, skills, abilities, and experiences to support your answers to the supplemental questions. UNC Charlotte Benefits Information: https://hr.charlotte.edu/benefits/benefits-overview/ Posting Open Date 09/15/2026 Posting Close Date 10/05/2026 Open Until Filled No Proposed Hire Date If time-limited please indicate appointment end date Contact Information Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? UNC Charlotte Website HERC Job Board Inside Higher Education Circa (formerly known as Local JobNetwork) Another Website Agency Referral Advertisement/Publication Personal Referral Other Where did you learn about this posting? (Open Ended Question) * Do you have a Master's degree in higher education administration, business, human resources, or a related field with commensurate experience? Yes, I have a Master's degree in higher education administration, business, human resources, or a related field with commensurate experience No, I do not have a Master's degree in higher education administration, business, human resources, or a related field with commensurate experience * Do you have progressive professional experience in employer relations, career services, business development, account/relationship management, or a comparable relationship-driven field? Yes, I have progressive professional experience in employer relations, career services, business development, account/relationship management, or a comparable relationship-driven field. No, I do not have progressive professional experience in employer relations, career services, business development, account/relationship management, or a comparable relationship-driven field. * Do you have experience directly supervising and developing staff, including performance management and goal-setting? Yes, I have experience directly supervising and developing staff, including performance management and goal-setting. No, I do not have experience directly supervising and developing staff, including performance management and goal-setting. Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume / Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Contact Information for References Optional Documents Other Document 9201 University City Blvd \r\nCharlotte, NC 28223 © 2026 The University of North Carolina at Charlotte. All rights reserved. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.charlotte.edu/postings/70509": {
      "title": "Assistant Director",
      "description": "UNC Charlotte Applicant Site | Assistant Director - Industry Specialist Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Frequently Asked Questions Application Process State of NC Salary Chart Campus Security Report Student Employment Assistant Director - Industry Specialist Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. The finalist will be subject to a Criminal Background Check and/or a Motor Vehicle Report The Search Committee will not contact references without first verifying permission with the finalist . Please ensure your resume reflects the knowledge, skills, abilities, and experiences to support your answers to the supplemental questions. UNC Charlotte Benefits Information: https://hr.charlotte.edu/benefits/benefits-overview/ Position Information General Information Position Number 000789 Vacancy Open to All Candidates Working Title Assistant Director - Industry Specialist Position Designation EHRA Non-Faculty Employment Type Permanent - Full-time Months per Year 12 Work Schedule Monday – Friday, 8:00 am to 5:00 pm, some evenings and weekends as required. Hours per week 40 FLSA Status Exempt Division Academic Affairs Department University College (Adm) Work Location Career Center Salary Range $62,000 Primary Purpose of Department The Career Center is committed to providing comprehensive, innovative services and resources for students, alumni, and employers that prepare UNC Charlotte graduates for the competitive global market. Through a focus on early, continuous career and professional preparation, the Career Center bridges academic knowledge and professional development. The Career Center seeks campus and employer partnerships to connect students with meaningful, real-world experiences, leading to success for both UNC Charlotte alumni and the greater Charlotte community. Primary Purpose of Position This position develops intensive, focused, and purposeful employer relationships within the Healthcare, Science, and Research sectors, in support of internships, experiential learning opportunities, shadowing, networking, and full-time jobs for students interested in those industries. The majority of this position’s time is dedicated to building and maintaining employer relationships within these assigned sectors. The Assistant Director also manages a team of students who support the broader Employer Engagement team’s employer sourcing and prospecting efforts, helping identify new contacts, target companies, and alumni connections across all industry focus areas. This position may also serve as instructor of record for up to one academic course per semester, as needed. Summary of Position Responsibilities Industry Relationship Development & Management Serves as the primary employer relationship manager for the Healthcare, Science, and Research sectors, developing new relationships with specific outcomes relating to internships, experiential learning opportunities, shadowing, and full-time jobs for students interested in these industries. Builds a strong pipeline of employer opportunities related to health, science, and research academic programs. Conducts data mining and lead generation for prospective employers relevant to the Healthcare, Science, and Research sectors, including contact with off-campus employers regionally and statewide. Works with employers across the Healthcare, Science, and Research sectors, gathering information on employment trends and professional skill needs; shares information with career advising staff and the campus community through trainings, meetings, and marketing. Maintains accurate and up-to-date employer relationship information in the team’s CRM , consistent with Employer Engagement team standards. Represents the Employer Engagement team at Healthcare, Science, and Research industry events, conferences, and professional associations. Programming, Networking & Shadowing Develops and implements shadowing and informational-interviewing opportunities connecting students to professionals in Healthcare, Science, and Research fields. Assists in the development and implementation of networking programs with a strong alumni presence, including shadowing/informational interviewing programs and newly created partnerships with key personnel across the University. Spearheads the development of company- and geography-focused learning and networking opportunities within Healthcare, Science, and Research, utilizing partnerships with parents, alumni, and other external partners. Coordinates career programming, panels, and events with the College of Science, College of Health and Human Services, and other relevant academic departments. Assists in the staffing of campus career fairs each year. Program Management — Employer Sourcing Student Team Recruits, trains, and supervises a team of students whose primary role is to support the Employer Engagement team’s employer sourcing and prospecting efforts across all industry focus areas. Directs the student team’s research to identify who the team should reach out to next, which companies would be good targets for new relationships, and which companies current alumni work at where the University does not yet have an employer relationship. Develops workflows and tools for the student team to track sourcing leads and routes findings to the appropriate Employer Engagement team member by industry focus. Makes the student sourcing team’s research and output available to the full Employer Engagement team, not solely to this position’s own industry portfolio. Specialized Projects/Other Responsibilities Researches and stays informed on hiring practices, employment trends, and other labor-related issues within Healthcare, Science, and Research; shares lessons learned with the entire Employer Engagement team. Assists as needed in the review and approval of job postings, informational session requests, and on-campus recruitment requests within assigned industry sectors. Assists in the staffing of employer on-campus events such as information sessions, networking events, and other employer/student connecting programs. Assists in the collection of relevant data to support office trending analysis, reports, and student learning. Participates in University events, including orientations, open houses, and other functions, to promote and represent the University Career Center. Assists the Employer Engagement team with other projects as assigned. Minimum Education/Experience Bachelor’s in human resources, business development, marketing, or other relevant degree required and 3 years of direct experience; or an equivalent combination of education and experience. Preferred Education, Knowledge, Skills and Experience Ability to work with individuals and groups and prepare and deliver high-quality, effective presentations. Must be proficient with technology such as CRM management, social media, or other recruitment-related software and interested in identifying and adopting technological advances in the field. Familiarity with, or strong interest in developing familiarity with, the Healthcare, Science, and Research employment landscape, including relevant employers, credentialing pathways, and industry trends. Well-developed interpersonal, marketing, and communication skills. Must be able to make decisions and work independently, as well as in team situations, including the supervision of student staff. Necessary Certifications/Licenses Preferred Certifications/Licenses Special Notes to Applicants The finalist will be subject to a Criminal Background Check and/or a Motor Vehicle Report The Search Committee will not contact references without first verifying permission with the finalist . Please ensure your resume reflects the knowledge, skills, abilities, and experiences to support your answers to the supplemental questions. UNC Charlotte Benefits Information: https://hr.charlotte.edu/benefits/benefits-overview/ Posting Open Date 09/15/2026 Posting Close Date 10/05/2026 Open Until Filled No Proposed Hire Date If time-limited please indicate appointment end date Contact Information Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? UNC Charlotte Website HERC Job Board Inside Higher Education Mitratech Circa (formerly known as Local JobNetwork) Another Website Agency Referral Advertisement/Publication Personal Referral Other Where did you learn about this posting? (Open Ended Question) * Do you have a Bachelor’s degree in human resources, business development, marketing, or other relevant degree required and 3 years of direct experience; or an equivalent combination of education and experience? Yes, I have a Bachelors Degree in human resources, business development, marketing, or other relevant degree required and three (3) years of direct experience; or an equivalent combination of education and experience. Yes, I have an Associates Degree in human resources, business development, marketing, or other relevant degree required and five (5) years of direct experience; or an equivalent combination of education and experience Yes, I have a High School Diploma/GED and seven (7) years of direct experience; or an equivalent combination of education and experience No, I do not Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume / Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Contact Information for References Optional Documents Other Document 9201 University City Blvd \r\nCharlotte, NC 28223 © 2026 The University of North Carolina at Charlotte. All rights reserved. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
