    "https://jobs.charlotte.edu/postings/70515": {
      "title": "Position Information",
      "description": "UNC Charlotte Applicant Site | Building Environmental Supervisor Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Frequently Asked Questions Application Process State of NC Salary Chart Campus Security Report Student Employment Building Environmental Supervisor Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Information General Information Vacancy Open to All Candidates Employment Type Permanent - Full-time If time-limited, note appointment end date Hours per week 40 Months per year 12 Position Number 011028 NC Salary Grade Equivalency NC07 Classification Title Building Environmental Supervisor - Journey Working Title Building Environmental Supervisor Salary  Range $40,304 - $55,418 Anticipate Hiring Range $40,304 - $50,380 FLSA Status Non Exempt Division Student Affairs Department Housing and Residence Life (Adm) Work Unit Housing and Residence Life Work Schedule 7:00 am – 3:30 pm; Monday – Friday with ‘on-call’ designation. Some weekend work required. Mandatory Employee This position is designated as ‘mandatory’ and, when contacted to report to work, its incumbent is expected to reach the campus as expeditiously as possible using normal precautions as dictated by the adverse weather conditions. Primary Purpose of Position The primary purpose of this position is to provide supervision of general cleaning responsibilities consistent with the standards set by Housing and Residence Life. This position will include area supervision for 2-3 residential complexes, up to 12 employees with additional temporary staff in summer, and training of staff on procedures and new products or equipment. Minimum Education/Experience Required Minimum Qualifications: Graduation from high school or possession of a GED , and one (1) year of experience in the area assigned; or an equivalent combination of education and experience. Note: Some state job postings state you can qualify by an ‘equivalent combination of education and experience.’ If that language appears above, then you may qualify through EITHER years of education OR years of directly related experience, OR a combination of both. Essential Job Duties The primary purpose of this position is to provide supervision of Building Environmental Technicians’ general cleaning responsibilities, consistent with the standards set by Housing and Residence Life. This position will include area supervision for 2-3 residential complexes, up to 8 employees, with additional temporary staff in the summer, and training staff on procedures and new products and equipment. Other Work Responsibilities Departmental Preferred Experience, Skills, Training/Education Experience professionally cleaning in a commercial or residential setting, such as a school, college, university, or hotel. Able to demonstrate cleaning skills. Able to work autonomously. Able to follow instructions. Able to lead team members and create a positive working environment. Able to effectively use technology. Necessary Licenses or Certifications Where applicable, must be eligible for required certification. Work Location Varies Posting date 09/16/2026 Closing date 09/23/2026 Proposed Hire Date 10/20/2026 Contact Information LaCrystal Jones Special Notes to Applicants Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? UNC Charlotte Website HERC Job Board Inside Higher Education Mitratech Circa (formerly known as Local JobNetwork) Another Website Agency Referral Advertisement/Publication Personal Referral Other Where did you learn about this posting? (Open Ended Question) * Do you have at least a high school diploma / GED and one year of related office experience or an equivalent combination of education and experience? Yes - I have at least a high school diploma / GED and one year of related office experience or an equivalent combination of education and experience No - I do not 