and cleans the examining area, monitors the flow of patients, follows up on missed appointments, and carries out Physician orders. Provide patient education and counseling. Minimum Education/Experience Required Minimum Qualifications: Possession of a current North Carolina license to practice as a Practical Nurse. Note: Some state job postings state you can qualify by an ‘equivalent combination of education and experience.’ If that language appears above, then you may qualify through EITHER years of education OR years of directly related experience, OR a combination of both. Essential Job Duties Provides nursing care for patients presenting to the medical clinic at Student Health. Performs patient intakes, including vital signs, for patients presenting for appointments with a healthcare provider in the medical clinic. Assist the provider with procedures, carries out provider orders such as medication administration and other treatments. Other Work Responsibilities Participates in on-campus health and wellbeing events such as vaccine clinics and health fairs. Departmental Preferred Experience, Skills, Training/Education Recent experience providing direct nursing care in an outpatient healthcare setting. Experience using electronic medical records Demonstrated excellence in customer service Experience providing nursing care to a college-aged population Necessary Licenses or Certifications Licensed to practice as a Practical Nurse in the State of North Carolina. Work Location Student Health Center Posting date 07/13/2026 Closing date 10/04/2026 Proposed Hire Date 10/26/2026 Contact Information Special Notes to Applicants This position is being reopened to attract a larger candidate pool. If you have already applied for this position, you do not need to reapply, as your application is still valid. The finalist will be subject to a Criminal Background Check and/or a Motor Vehicle Report The Search Committee will not contact references without first verifying permission with the finalist . Please ensure your application reflects the knowledge, skills, abilities, and experiences to support your answers to the supplemental questions. Do not write ‘see resume’ on your application when completing the job duties section. UNC Charlotte Benefits Information: https://hr.charlotte.edu/benefits/benefits-overview/ Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? UNC Charlotte Website HERC Job Board Inside Higher Education Mitratech Circa (formerly known as Local JobNetwork) Another Website Agency Referral Advertisement/Publication Personal Referral Other Where did you learn about this posting? (Open Ended Question) * Are you licensed to practice as a Practical Nurse in the State of North Carolina? No Yes * Do you have direct nursing care in an outpatient healthcare setting and experience using electronic medical records? (Open Ended Question) * Do you have experience providing nursing care to college aged population? If yes, please briefly describe your experience. (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume / Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Optional Documents Contact Information for References 9201 University City Blvd \r\nCharlotte, NC 28223 © 2026 The University of North Carolina at Charlotte. All rights reserved. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
