    "https://jobs.charlotte.edu/postings/70674": {
      "title": "Department Chair & Professor",
      "description": "UNC Charlotte Applicant Site | Department Chair &amp; Professor Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Frequently Asked Questions Application Process State of NC Salary Chart Campus Security Report Student Employment Department Chair & Professor Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. This posting is open to UNC Charlotte employees only. Position Information General Information Position Number 005119 Working Title Department Chair & Professor Classification Title Department Chair/ Director College Col of Arts & Architecture (Col) Department Theatre Position Designation Faculty Employment Type Permanent - Full-time Months per year 12 Primary Purpose of Department The Department of Theatre inspires students to expand their vision of the world and themselves through the study and practice of theatre. The Department offers a B.A. in Theatre with concentrations available in design and production, performance, or theatre education. Our student-centered, community-engaged education in theatre fosters the development of “cross-trained artists” who are prepared to participate in professional theatre as well as any profession that places value on imaginative thinking, collaboration, and communication skills. The program creates intellectual and creative experiences for students through rigorous classroom instruction and innovative approaches to stage production. The faculty comprises nationally recognized scholars and artists who mentor students through individual projects as well as collaborative works that embrace a wide range of aesthetic perspectives, and innovative creative research practices. Vacancy Open to UNC Charlotte Employees Only Description of Work Responsible for the daily operation of the department and the department programs. The Department Chair/ Director will promote excellence in department programs within the University. Chair/ Director responsibilities are classified as professional duties requiring leadership and mentoring of faculty, administrative expertise to include vision, long term and short-term planning, decision-making and coordination of instruction. If this position conducts research, the following statement is applicable: This position is subject to research-security screening. As part of the application, applicants must disclose, either in their CV or in a separate document submitted with the application , all current appointments or affiliations with foreign institutions or organizations, foreign research support, and ongoing research collaborations with foreign institutions, organizations, or their personnel. Before candidates advance to an on-campus interview, the university will review this information and other publicly available information for relationships involving institutions on the current Section 1286 list and any other applicable U.S. restricted-party lists. A disclosed or identified relationship does not automatically disqualify a candidate. As a condition of employment, a selected candidate must resolve any relationship the university determines would violate applicable law or sponsor requirements or materially impair the candidate’s or the university’s eligibility for federal funding. Essential Duties and Responsibilities The Chair reports to the Dean of the CoA+A, sets Departmental priorities in consultation with the faculty, provides leadership in strategic planning, administers Departmental and College policies, and assumes final responsibility for Departmental and production budgets, planning documents, self‐studies, and annual reports. The Chair takes an active role in, and assumes final responsibility for hiring all faculty and administrative staff. The Chair is responsible for assigning faculty workloads, individual course schedules, service assignments, annual reviews of all full time faculty, and provides guidance in RPT , PTR and other processes. The Chair also assumes final responsibility for the production season schedules and works collaboratively with the Associate Dean for Production Arts Operations on production support and the use of performance spaces. The Chair represents the Department to the Dean and the Provost & Vice Chancellor for Academic Affairs, and serves as a liaison to the arts community beyond the University. Minimum Experience/Education UNC Charlotte gives primary consideration to the earned doctorate or terminal degree in the teaching discipline or a related discipline. Preferred Education, Skills and Experience Successful candidates will display an energetic and collaborative leadership style that inspires faculty, students, and staff to develop a shared vision for the future of the Department of Theatre. Candidates are sought who demonstrate leadership in 21st century approaches to Theatre, evidence of leadership in advancing innovation in pedagogy, performance, research, partnership building, administration, and in the workplace. Successful candidates will also possess excellent interpersonal and communication skills and the ability to recruit, mentor, and support faculty and students of many different backgrounds. Successful candidates may have experience with community-based, site-specific, devised, and/or collaborative work, and an understanding and appreciation for the variety of approaches, perspectives, and specializations that comprise research in Theatre. This may include an ability to advocate for the value of research in and resources for Theatre, in all its forms, relative to UNC Charlotte’s unique role as an R1 Urban Research University. Candidates may also have qualifications that include arts administration, fundraising, and artistic or managerial experience in professional theatre. This is a tenured position; eligibility for tenure rank (Associate or Full Professor) will depend on the background and experience of the candidate. Necessary Licenses/Certifications The successful candidate will hold a terminal degree in Theatre or related field and have a record of significant professional activity suitable for appointment at the rank of Associate or Full Professor, as well as a proven record of academic and professional leadership. Special Notes to Applicants This posting is open to UNC Charlotte employees only. Job Open Date 09/23/2026 Job Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Date Review of Applications will Begin 10/15/2026 Proposed Hire Date 07/01/2027 If time-limited, please indicate appointment end date Contact Information Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Resume / Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents 9201 University City Blvd \r\nCharlotte, NC 28223 © 2026 The University of North Carolina at Charlotte. All rights reserved. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.charlotte.edu/postings/70579": {
      "title": "Operations Coordinator",
      "description": "UNC Charlotte Applicant Site | Operations Coordinator Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Frequently Asked Questions Application Process State of NC Salary Chart Campus Security Report Student Employment Operations Coordinator Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. UNC Charlotte Benefits Information: https://hr.charlotte.edu/benefits/benefits-overview/ The finalist will be subject to a Criminal Background Check and/or a Motor Vehicle Report. Please ensure your application reflects the knowledge, skills, abilities, and experiences to support your answers to the supplemental questions (see the job duties section of previous employment). Please submit a resume and cover letter with your application. These documents will be used to evaluate your written communication skills as well as supporting documents of your knowledge, skills, abilities, education, and professional experience. Please upload reference information, including ​names, position titles, and company/institutions, phone numbers, and email addresses of at least ​two​ current/previous supervisors. The Search Committee will not contact references without first verifying permission with the finalist . Position Information General Information Vacancy Open to All Candidates Employment Type Permanent - Full-time If time-limited, note appointment end date Hours per week 40 Months per year 12 Position Number 013015 NC Salary Grade Equivalency NC07 Classification Title Building Environmental Supervisor - Journey Working Title Operations Coordinator Salary  Range $40,304- $55,418 Anticipate Hiring Range $40,304 - $50,380 FLSA Status Non Exempt Division Athletics Department Athletics Venues (Adm) Work Unit Student Activity Ctr and Venue Mgmt Work Schedule 7:00 am – 4:00 pm, with varying days off in conjunction with event schedules. Work hours may also include evening, weekend, and holiday hours as necessary to accommodate event coverage Mandatory Position This position is designated as ‘mandatory’ during adverse weather or emergency events, and when contacted to report to work, the employee is expected to reach the campus as quickly as possible using normal precautions as dictated by adverse weather conditions. In the event of an area disaster, the Student Activity Center may be designated for use as an emergency shelter or for emergency operations. Primary Purpose of Position This position serves as an Operations Coordinator, with responsibility for oversight of the daily operations of Halton Arena, including housekeeping, event setup (large/small), inventory management, and all associated safety guideline compliance and enforcement. Work responsibilities may also be associated with other athletic facilities, as appropriate or necessary. Minimum Education/Experience Required Minimum Qualifications: Graduation from high school or possession of a GED , and one (1) year of experience in the area assigned; or an equivalent combination of education and experience. Note: Some state job postings state you can qualify by an ‘equivalent combination of education and experience.’ If that language appears above, then you may qualify through EITHER years of education OR years of directly related experience, OR a combination of both. Essential Job Duties Work with a 3rd-party contracted cleaning company and Maintenance supervisors to effectively communicate expectations of the department and facilities to the department. Establish rules, standards, guidelines, and policies governing the quality and quantity of work. Determine work priorities and timelines for staff as it relates to daily work, projects, and event support. Ensure proper planning for set-ups, equipment, and staffing to support daily operations and events. Determine and develop training sessions necessary for employees for safety/security and equipment best practices. Assist the Senior Director of Operations with inventory of all equipment and 49er Mart purchases of supplies for all athletic facilities. Manage all shipping and receiving of items and equipment for the facility. Manage storage space in the facility Responsible for all training on equipment for staff Work with Supervisors to determine objectives, establish work standards, and set expectations & goals to meet facility needs consistently Maintain an up-to-date equipment inventory for all facility equipment and assist in performing annual inventory in conjunction with UNC Charlotte Assess equipment needs and make recommendations to the Senior Director for Operations on replacement Serve as Operations Manager on Duty for Events as assigned, including – Volleyball Games/Women’s Basketball/Cheerleading/Jiu-Jitsu Any major events as needed Liaise with the Senior Director of Operations and team members to optimize schedules and address staffing needs. Monitor staff availability and adjust shifts as necessary to meet operational demands. Master Checklists: Creating and maintaining task assignments and standard operating procedures (SOPs) for staff. Time Management: Meeting tight pre- and post-game deadlines in a high-pressure, fast-paced environment. Manage and Coordinate usage of rapid Salon floor diagram set-ups and changeovers for Events. Other Work Responsibilities Departmental Preferred Experience, Skills, Training/Education Experience in an Athletic Arena or Conference Center setting. Necessary Licenses or Certifications Where applicable, must be eligible for the required certification. Work Location All Athletic Facilities Posting date 09/18/2026 Closing date 09/27/2026 Proposed Hire Date 10/19/2026 Contact Information Special Notes to Applicants UNC Charlotte Benefits Information: https://hr.charlotte.edu/benefits/benefits-overview/ The finalist will be subject to a Criminal Background Check and/or a Motor Vehicle Report. Please ensure your application reflects the knowledge, skills, abilities, and experiences to support your answers to the supplemental questions (see the job duties section of previous employment). Please submit a resume and cover letter with your application. These documents will be used to evaluate your written communication skills as well as supporting documents of your knowledge, skills, abilities, education, and professional experience. Please upload reference information, including ​names, position titles, and company/institutions, phone numbers, and email addresses of at least ​two​ current/previous supervisors. The Search Committee will not contact references without first verifying permission with the finalist . Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). How did you hear about this employment opportunity? UNC Charlotte Website HERC Job Board Inside Higher Education Mitratech Circa (formerly known as Local JobNetwork) Another Website Agency Referral Advertisement/Publication Personal Referral Other Where did you learn about this posting? (Open Ended Question) * Do you have at least a high school diploma or GED and at least 1 year of experience in the area assigned OR an equivalent combination of education and experience? Yes No * Do you have experience in an Athletic Arena or Conference Center setting? Please explain. (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume / Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Contact Information for References Optional Documents 9201 University City Blvd \r\nCharlotte, NC 28223 © 2026 The University of North Carolina at Charlotte. All rights reserved. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.charlotte.edu/postings/70676": {
      "title": "Administrative Support Associate",
      "description": "UNC Charlotte Applicant Site | Administrative Support Associate Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Frequently Asked Questions Application Process State of NC Salary Chart Campus Security Report Student Employment Administrative Support Associate Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. The finalist will be subject to a Criminal Background Check and/or a Motor Vehicle Report The Search Committee will not contact references without first verifying permission with the finalist . Please ensure your application reflects the knowledge, skills, abilities, and experiences to support your answers to the supplemental questions. Do not write ‘see resume’ on your application when completing the job duties section. UNC Charlotte Benefits Information: https://hr.charlotte.edu/benefits/benefits-overview/ Position Information General Information Vacancy Open to All Candidates Employment Type Permanent - Full-time If time-limited, note appointment end date Hours per week 40 Months per year 12 Position Number 006010 NC Salary Grade Equivalency NC03 Classification Title Administrative Support Associate - Advanced Working Title Administrative Support Associate Salary  Range $35,212 - $48,417 Anticipate Hiring Range $35,212 - $44,015 FLSA Status Non Exempt Division Academic Affairs Department College of Humanities & Earth and Social Sciences (Col) Work Unit Col of Hum & Earth and Social Sci Work Schedule 8:00 am – 5:00 pm; Monday – Friday Primary Purpose of Position The position serves as Administrative Assistant for the CHESS Office of Finance & Personnel (F&P) and is responsible for monitoring and maintaining the College’s Office of Academic Technology budget and other assigned college sub-unit budgets. The position facilitates financial and administrative transactions for the Dean’s Office; coordinates the scheduling and management of F&P-related meetings, committees, and working groups; and coordinates F&P communications with CHESS departments, other campus units, and external constituencies. The position also performs a variety of administrative tasks and special projects in support of the Assistant Dean for Finance & Personnel; provides customer service and administrative support to students, faculty, staff, and visitors; and provides administrative support to college units, as assigned, during periods of staff vacancies. The position also serves as Office Manager, supporting the day-to-day administrative operations of the office. Minimum Education/Experience Required Minimum Qualifications: Graduation from high school or an equivalent combination of education and experience. Note: Some state job postings state you can qualify by an ‘equivalent combination of education and experience.’ If that language appears above, then you may qualify through EITHER years of education OR years of directly related experience, OR a combination of both. Essential Job Duties Serve as Administrative Assistant/Office Manager for the CHESS Office of Finance & Personnel (F&P) and be responsible for monitoring and maintaining the College’s Office of Academic Technology budget and other assigned college sub-unit budgets, as well as supporting the day-to-day administrative operations of the office. Greet, assist, and direct guests, visitors, and students of the CHESS Office of Finance & Personnel. Remain calm and professional in all verbal communications with internal and external constituencies. Apply knowledge of programs, policies, and procedures to interpret and communicate information to meet the specific needs of students, faculty, and staff. Coordinate Finance & Personnel (F&P) meetings, training, working groups, and special projects, including scheduling, space reservations, materials, communications, and follow-up. Provide administrative coordination for recurring F&P activities, including departmental budget reviews, Business Update meetings, and other College-wide administrative functions as assigned. Track multiple assignments, deadlines, requests, and action items and follow up with responsible parties to support timely completion. Prepare and coordinate routine administrative transactions and documentation, including reimbursements, travel, direct/special payments, and other forms as assigned. Serve as the primary administrative coordinator for Finance & Personnel records management, maintaining organized electronic and hard-copy filing systems for financial, personnel, and administrative records. Maintain and update administrative spreadsheets, tracking tools, reference materials, recurring reports, and electronic repositories used by the Finance & Personnel Office. Retrieve and compile information from University systems and repositories; identify missing, incomplete, or inconsistent records and coordinate resolution with appropriate staff. Adhere to privacy and confidentiality policies to safeguard personnel and student information (i.e., FERPA and HIPAA ). Serve as a resource for faculty and staff relating to travel, purchasing, and other university processes and procedures. Utilize conflict management techniques to resolve issues efficiently. Collaborate with other team members in order to de-escalate situations and solve problems. Complete 49er Requests, Purchase Orders, EPAF payments, and e-forms for the Office of Finance & Personnel, and other administrators in the Dean’s Office, as needed. Serve as Concur Delegate for all staff in the Office of Finance & Personnel. May serve as delegate in other departments when vacancies arise. Utilize Concur to reconcile P-Card expenses as needed. Other Work Responsibilities Assist in the planning, development, and execution of special projects. Coordinate administrative onboarding requirements for newly hired Dean’s Office employees, including equipment, keys, parking, supplies, and related operational needs. Coordinate the scheduling and management of F&P-related meetings, committees, and working groups. Coordinate F&P communications with CHESS departments, other campus units, and external constituencies. Research and recommend office equipment and software that would positively affect workflow and effectiveness. Maintain and create spreadsheets in MS Excel and/or Google Suite to enter data and generate reports. Utilize Banner, 49er Mart, Kronos, and other systems as designated. Attend appropriate training sessions and complete web modules. Create Travel Requests, Expense Reports, and prepare reimbursements in Concur. Other duties, as assigned. Departmental Preferred Experience, Skills, Training/Education Administrative experience working in Higher Education is preferred. Financial management/budget experience and proactive organizational skills are a plus. Intermediate knowledge and skills in the use of the Microsoft Office Suite, Google software, and university systems such as Banner, Concur, Report Central, or similar are highly desired. Ability to work independently, with a high level of professionalism, customer service orientation, and an understanding of confidentiality is strongly preferred. Excellent written and oral communication skills and strong attention to detail are preferred. Necessary Licenses or Certifications Work Location Fretwell - Suite 326 Posting date 09/22/2026 Closing date 09/29/2026 Proposed Hire Date 10/26/2026 Contact Information Special Notes to Applicants The finalist will be subject to a Criminal Background Check and/or a Motor Vehicle Report The Search Committee will not contact references without first verifying permission with the finalist . Please ensure your application reflects the knowledge, skills, abilities, and experiences to support your answers to the supplemental questions. Do not write ‘see resume’ on your application when completing the job duties section. UNC Charlotte Benefits Information: https://hr.charlotte.edu/benefits/benefits-overview/ Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? UNC Charlotte Website HERC Job Board Inside Higher Education Mitratech Circa (formerly known as Local JobNetwork) Another Website Agency Referral Advertisement/Publication Personal Referral Other Where did you learn about this posting? (Open Ended Question) * Do you have a High School Diploma/GED; or an equivalent combination of education and experience? Yes No * Do you have professional administrative experience working in a college and/or university setting? No Yes * Do you have professional financial management and budget experience? Yes No Knowledge of with limited experience * Do you have experience working with campus systems including 49er Mart, Banner, Concur, etc? Please provide examples: (Open Ended Question) * Please explain your level of proficiency with Microsoft Office and Google Workspace. (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume / Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Optional Documents Contact Information for References 9201 University City Blvd \r\nCharlotte, NC 28223 © 2026 The University of North Carolina at Charlotte. All rights reserved. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
