    "https://jobs.charlotte.edu/postings/70638": {
      "title": "Assistant Director of Operations",
      "description": "UNC Charlotte Applicant Site | Assistant Director of Operations Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Frequently Asked Questions Application Process State of NC Salary Chart Campus Security Report Student Employment Assistant Director of Operations Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. The finalist will be subject to a Criminal Background Check and/or a Motor Vehicle Report. The Search Committee will not contact references without first verifying permission with the finalist. Please ensure your resume reflects the knowledge, skills, abilities, and experiences to support your answers to the supplemental questions. UNC Charlotte Benefits Information: https://hr.charlotte.edu/benefits/benefits-overview/ Position Information General Information Position Number 001018 Vacancy Open to All Candidates Working Title Assistant Director of Operations Position Designation EHRA Non-Faculty Employment Type Permanent - Full-time Months per Year 12 Work Schedule Monday – Friday, 8:00 am – 5:00 pm. Nights and weekends are required occasionally. Hours per week 40 FLSA Status Exempt Division Academic Affairs Department Enrollment Management (Adm) Work Location Gage Undergraduate Admissions Center Salary Range $50,000 - $55,482 Primary Purpose of Department The mission of the Undergraduate Admissions Office is to meet the established University enrollment goals by recruiting undergraduate applicants. Our goal is to recruit applicants who can contribute to and profit from the University in academic programs and activities; assist prospects and applicants in realizing their academic ambitions through counseling; accurately and efficiently review academic credentials and notify applicants of decisions; and provide the University community with data necessary for advising and enrollment planning. Our mission statement is “to provide quality service, promote quality service, promote educational opportunities and facilitate enrollment at the University”. We value our position as the first contact a prospective student or the general public may have with the University. Providing timely and accurate information and effectively monitoring the admissions process is critical to the successful recruitment of qualified students. Functionally, the office staff works closely with the faculty and support units on campus and with high school counselors, parents, and community college counselors off-campus Primary Purpose of Position The Assistant Director of Operations provides leadership and oversight for operational functions within the Office of Undergraduate Admissions, with a primary focus on application processing, academic credential evaluation, and workflow management. Reporting to the Associate Director of Operations, this position supervises a team of three Academic Credential Evaluators and ensures timely, accurate, and efficient review of undergraduate applications in support of institutional enrollment goals. The Assistant Director plays a key role in maintaining operational excellence, improving business processes, ensuring compliance with university and state policies, and supporting a student-centered admissions experience. Summary of Position Responsibilities Supervise, train, mentor, and evaluate a team of three Academic Credential Evaluators. Oversee the review and evaluation of domestic and/or international academic credentials for undergraduate admission. Assist in maintaining data integrity within the student information system and admissions CRM platforms. Analyze operational processes and recommend improvements to increase efficiency, accuracy, and service delivery. Ensure adherence to university, state, federal, and accreditation regulations related to admissions processing and student records. Partner with campus stakeholders, including Enrollment Management, Registrar, Information Technology, Institutional Research, and academic colleges to support admissions operations. Other Information about this role: Standard office environment with extended periods of computer use. Occasional evening or weekend work during peak admissions periods. Hybrid work eligibility may be available based on departmental needs and university policy. Minimum Education/Experience Bachelor’s degree from an accredited institution. Three years of progressively responsible experience in admissions operations, credential evaluation, enrollment management, or a related higher education function. Preferred Education, Knowledge, Skills and Experience Master’s degree in Higher Education, Business Administration, Public Administration, or a related field, or 3 years of relevant experience Strong leadership and staff management capabilities. Experience with large public university admissions operations. Familiarity with domestic and international credential evaluation practices. Experience using systems such as Banner, Slate, PeopleSoft, or similar enterprise platforms. Knowledge of FERPA and higher education compliance standards. Demonstrated ability to implement process improvements and operational efficiencies. Necessary Certifications/Licenses Preferred Certifications/Licenses Special Notes to Applicants The finalist will be subject to a Criminal Background Check and/or a Motor Vehicle Report. The Search Committee will not contact references without first verifying permission with the finalist. Please ensure your resume reflects the knowledge, skills, abilities, and experiences to support your answers to the supplemental questions. UNC Charlotte Benefits Information: https://hr.charlotte.edu/benefits/benefits-overview/ Posting Open Date 09/21/2026 Posting Close Date 10/05/2026 Open Until Filled No Proposed Hire Date 10/26/2026 If time-limited please indicate appointment end date Contact Information Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? UNC Charlotte Website HERC Job Board Inside Higher Education Mitratech Circa (formerly known as Local JobNetwork) Another Website Agency Referral Advertisement/Publication Personal Referral Other Where did you learn about this posting? (Open Ended Question) * Do you have a bachelor’s degree from an accredited institution with three years of progressively responsible experience in admissions operations, credential evaluation, enrollment management, or a related higher education function? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume / Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Contact Information for References Optional Documents 9201 University City Blvd \r\nCharlotte, NC 28223 © 2026 The University of North Carolina at Charlotte. All rights reserved. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
