    "https://jobs.charlotte.edu/postings/70564": {
      "title": "Enrollment Services Specialist",
      "description": "UNC Charlotte Applicant Site | Enrollment Services Specialist Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Frequently Asked Questions Application Process State of NC Salary Chart Campus Security Report Student Employment Enrollment Services Specialist Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. You don't have to already know Financial Aid + Registration + Student Accounts + Residency - that’s helpful if you do, but we can train. You do need to demonstrate that you can learn complex information, interpret rules, navigate numerous technology applications, exercise judgment, communicate exceptionally well, and function effectively under significant demand. This posting will be used to fill four positions, 001943, 001941, 001949, and 008042. The finalist will be subject to a Criminal Background Check and/or a Motor Vehicle Report The Search Committee will not contact references without first verifying permission with the finalist. Please ensure your application reflects the knowledge, skills, abilities, and experiences to support your answers to the supplemental questions. Do not write ‘see resume’ on your application when completing the job duties section. UNC Charlotte Benefits Information: https://hr.charlotte.edu/benefits/benefits-overview/ Position Information General Information Vacancy Open to All Candidates Employment Type Permanent - Full-time If time-limited, note appointment end date Hours per week 40 Months per year 12 Position Number 001943 NC Salary Grade Equivalency NC07 Classification Title Student Services Specialist - Journey Working Title Enrollment Services Specialist Salary  Range $39,058 - $53,705 Anticipate Hiring Range $39,058 - $48,823 FLSA Status Non Exempt Division Academic Affairs Department Enrollment Management (Adm) Work Unit Niner Central Work Schedule Standard 8-hour shifts are scheduled within Niner Central’s operating hours of 7:30 a.m. to 5:30 p.m., Monday through Friday , with a hybrid work schedule. This position may be eligible for a telework schedule once onboarding is complete and with supervisor approval. Occasional evening and weekend work is required to support recruitment, enrollment, and student events. This position may also be designated as essential personnel and required to report during university emergency or crisis operations as directed by the Chancellor. Primary Purpose of Position The Niner Central Enrollment Services Specialist provides comprehensive, student-centered support across Financial Aid, Registration, Student Accounts, Residency, and related university services. The position independently interprets and applies established policies, procedures, and requirements to resolve routine, complex, and non-standard student issues within delegated authority while providing coordinated, holistic guidance that supports student success. As a cross-functional resource, the position works across multiple Enrollment Management disciplines to identify related student needs, minimize unnecessary referrals, and promote first-contact resolution. The position also supports colleagues through knowledge sharing and training and contributes to service delivery, operational processes, outreach initiatives, and continuous improvement efforts that enhance the student experience. Minimum Education/Experience Required Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree; or equivalent combination of education and experience. All degrees must be received from appropriately accredited institutions. Note: Some state job postings state you can qualify by an ‘equivalent combination of education and experience.’ If that language appears above, then you may qualify through EITHER years of education OR years of directly related experience, OR a combination of both. Essential Job Duties Provides comprehensive, student-centered service across Financial Aid, Registration, Student Accounts, Residency, and related university services, delivering coordinated guidance and promoting first-contact resolution whenever possible. Independently interprets and applies established federal, state, UNC System, and University policies, regulations, procedures, and business processes to resolve routine, complex, and non-standard student issues within delegated authority. Reviews and analyzes student records, financial and enrollment information and related documentation across multiple university systems to identify issues, determine appropriate actions, and coordinate services that support student success. Delivers accurate, responsive, and professional service through multiple channels, including phone, email, chat, text, virtual appointments, and in-person interactions, using effective communication, active listening, conflict resolution, and de-escalation techniques. Coordinates with campus partners to resolve cross-functional issues and facilitates appropriate consultations, warm handoffs, and escalations while supporting continuity of service through resolution. Utilizes Salesforce, Banner, TouchNet, along with a high volume of other university, State of NC and federal systems to research and process student requests and maintain complete, accurate, and timely documentation of student records, interactions, and case activity. Identifies recurring student issues, service barriers, and operational trends and recommends improvements to processes, workflows, communications, technology, and service delivery. Supports organizational knowledge and operational consistency through onboarding, training, mentoring, knowledge sharing, and cross-training activities. Participates in departmental initiatives, projects, outreach activities, and program or technology enhancements by providing operational input, testing processes and system changes, identifying issues, and supporting implementation. Protects the confidentiality and integrity of student information and complies with applicable federal, state, UNC System, and University privacy, security, and records requirements, including FERPA and PCI requirements Supports recruitment, enrollment, orientation, registration, and other university events and operational needs as assigned. Other Work Responsibilities The successful candidate will demonstrate the ability to: Successfully complete required onboarding and training, demonstrate satisfactory progress through established training milestones and assessments. Achieve defined proficiency in assigned student service areas within 90 days following completion of initial training, as measured by established departmental performance, quality, accuracy, and knowledge standards. Build positive, professional relationships with students, families, colleagues, and campus partners through effective communication, empathy, collaboration, and a student-centered approach. Manage multiple priorities and competing demands in a fast-paced, technology-enabled environment while maintaining accuracy, productivity, attention to detail, and service quality. Apply critical thinking, sound judgment, and problem-solving skills to research issues, evaluate information, and determine appropriate actions within established policies, procedures, and delegated authority. Demonstrate adaptability and resilience in response to changing priorities, processes, technologies, service demands, and organizational needs while maintaining professionalism and accountability. Work collaboratively across functional areas, share knowledge, and expertise and contribute to a supportive team environment that promotes consistency, effective service delivery, and student success. Seek, receive, and apply constructive feedback and actively participate in ongoing learning, professional development, training, and cross-training to build and maintain proficiency across assigned service areas. Recognize and communicate opportunities to improve the student experience, service delivery, processes and operational effectiveness. Perform other duties and responsibilities as assigned to support departmental priorities, university initiatives, and evolving student and operational needs. Departmental Preferred Experience, Skills, Training/Education Experience in higher education, student services, enrollment management, financial aid, student accounts, registration, or a similarly complex service-oriented environment. Experience providing customer service in a high-volume, multi-channel environment using phone, email, chat, text, virtual, and/or in-person service channels. Experience interpreting and explaining policies, procedures, regulations, or complex information and applying established guidance to resolve customer or client issues, exercising sound judgment within established guidelines, and recognizing when consultation or escalation is appropriate. Strong written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to communicate complex information clearly, accurately, and in a customer-friendly manner. Experience using CRM , student information, case management, or other enterprise systems; experience with Salesforce, Banner, TouchNet, or similar systems is preferred. Necessary Licenses or Certifications Work Location 380 Cone Center Posting date 08/14/2026 Closing date 09/24/2026 Proposed Hire Date 10/19/2026 Contact Information Special Notes to Applicants You don’t have to already know Financial Aid + Registration + Student Accounts + Residency – that’s helpful if you do, but we can train. You do need to demonstrate that you can learn complex information, interpret rules, navigate numerous technology applications, exercise judgment, communicate exceptionally well, and function effectively under significant demand. This posting will be used to fill four positions, 001943, 001941, 001949, and 008042. The finalist will be subject to a Criminal Background Check and/or a Motor Vehicle Report The Search Committee will not contact references without first verifying permission with the finalist. Please ensure your application reflects the knowledge, skills, abilities, and experiences to support your answers to the supplemental questions. Do not write ‘see resume’ on your application when completing the job duties section. UNC Charlotte Benefits Information: https://hr.charlotte.edu/benefits/benefits-overview/ Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? UNC Charlotte Website HERC Job Board Inside Higher Education Mitratech Circa (formerly known as Local JobNetwork) Another Website Agency Referral Advertisement/Publication Personal Referral Other Where did you learn about this posting? (Open Ended Question) * Do you have a bachelor’s degree or equivalent combination of education and experience? All degrees must be received from appropriately accredited institutions. Yes, at least a bachelor's degree. Yes, an associate degree and 2 years of related work experience. Yes, a high school diploma/GED and 4 years of related work experience. No * Do you have customer service experience in a high-volume capacity? If so, please explain your experience. (Open Ended Question) * Describe your experience interpreting policies, procedures, or regulations to resolve customer or client issues. (Open Ended Question) * Please describe any experience you have working in higher education, student services, enrollment management, financial aid, registration, student accounts, or a related field. If you do not have higher education experience, describe a comparable environment where you provided complex customer support. (Open Ended Question) * Please describe your experience using customer relationship management (CRM) systems or other enterprise software (e.g., Salesforce, Banner, Workday, ServiceNow, PeopleSoft, etc.). Include the systems you have used and how you utilized them in your work (Open Ended Question) * This position requires simultaneously navigating multiple computer systems while providing service through phone, email, chat, and other communication channels. Please describe your experience managing multiple technologies while delivering accurate and timely customer service. (Open Ended Question) * This position requires the ability to work an assigned 8-hour shift scheduled between 7:30 a.m. and 5:30 p.m., Monday through Friday, with occasional evening and weekend hours to support recruitment, enrollment, and student events. Are you able to meet this scheduling requirement? Yes No * Please describe your experience working in a collaborative, team-based environment where you partnered across departments to resolve customer or client issues. (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume / Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Contact Information for References Optional Documents 9201 University City Blvd \r\nCharlotte, NC 28223 © 2026 The University of North Carolina at Charlotte. All rights reserved. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.charlotte.edu/postings/70655": {
      "title": "Position Information",
      "description": "UNC Charlotte Applicant Site | Employee Relations Consultant Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Frequently Asked Questions Application Process State of NC Salary Chart Campus Security Report Student Employment Employee Relations Consultant Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. The finalist will be subject to a Criminal Background Check and/or a Motor Vehicle Report The Search Committee will not contact references without first verifying permission with the finalist. Please ensure your resume reflects the knowledge, skills, abilities, and experiences to support your answers to the supplemental questions. UNC Charlotte Benefits Information: https://hr.charlotte.edu/benefits/benefits overview/ If there is a document you feel is relevant to this position that you would like reviewed with your resume and application, you may upload it to the \"Other Documents\" section of the Applicant Documents. Telework Schedule: This position is eligible for a hybrid work arrangement based on successful performance, conduct, completion of required training, and operational needs. After 90 days: Eligibility for up to one (1) remote workday per week . After six months: Consideration may be given for up to two (2) remote workdays per week , contingent upon successful completion of designated training and demonstrated satisfactory performance and conduct. Telework is not guaranteed and is subject to ongoing review and approval by Human Resources leadership. Telework arrangements may be modified or discontinued based on operational or business needs, performance or conduct considerations, or changes to University telework policies, procedures, and practices. Position Information General Information Position Number 000468 Vacancy Open to All Candidates Working Title Employee Relations Consultant Position Designation EHRA Non-Faculty Employment Type Permanent - Full-time Months per Year 12 Work Schedule 8:00 AM – 5:00 PM, Monday – Friday, with occasional evenings and weekend hours required, as necessary Hours per week 40 FLSA Status Exempt Division Business Affairs Department Human Resources (Adm) Work Location King Hall, 113 Salary Range $66,000 Primary Purpose of Department The Human Resources Department’s Employee Relations (ER) Unit supports a positive, productive, and fair work environment by providing comprehensive services to employees, managers, and supervisors. The office administers key programs and policies related to discipline, performance management, grievances, unemployment insurance, ADA workplace accommodations, and the prevention of unlawful workplace harassment, discrimination, or retaliation, as well as workplace violence. Our team offers counseling and guidance to employees who have workplace concerns, complaints, or grievances. We also provide consultative support to managers and supervisors, assisting with performance expectations, documentation, feedback, and the development and issuance of appropriate communications, including those related to disciplinary actions. Primary Purpose of Position The primary purpose of this position is to serve as a key Employee Relations Consultant for the university, managing and facilitating the day-to-day functions, ensuring compliance, consistency, and a supportive process. The ER Consultant’s role is dedicated to core employee relations responsibilities, including coaching and advising managers on performance and disciplinary matters up to and including termination; conducting investigations and grievance processes; facilitating conflict resolution between employees and/or managers; and proactively identifying opportunities to strengthen employee relations practices, procedures, and overall workplace culture. Additional responsibilities may include, but are not limited to, tracking and managing cases through the Salesforce Case Management and Ticketing system; assigning and responding to cases received through the Employee Relations and ADA email inboxes; writing investigation summaries and reports; answering phone calls and performing administrative tasks; and generating reports to support team operations and data-driven decision-making. Summary of Position Responsibilities This position serves as the primary point of contact for employees and department leaders (supervisors and managers) regarding employee relations matters. Key responsibilities include intake and resolution of employee complaints, administering disciplinary procedures, and reviewing and editing documentation such as written warnings, Performance Improvement Plans (PIPs), and related communications. Minimum Education/Experience Bachelor’s degree in human resources, business, psychology, organizational development, or a related field, and At least two years of progressively responsible experience analyzing, interpreting, applying, communicating, and promoting HR best practices in support of organizational goals and objectives; or An equivalent combination of relevant education, training, and experience. Preferred Education, Knowledge, Skills and Experience Four or more years of direct employee relations experience handling disciplinary matters, conducting investigations, and mediating workplace conflicts between employee-to-employee or employee-to-supervisor/manager. Experience documenting case activities and managing cases in a case management system (e.g., Salesforce, ServiceNow, Remedy, or SAP ). Demonstrated ability to manage an average caseload of approximately 15 employee relations cases simultaneously. Advanced proficiency in Microsoft Excel. Demonstrated ability to communicate effectively, both in writing and verbally, with diverse audiences, Necessary Certifications/Licenses Preferred Certifications/Licenses HR Certification ( SHRM -CP® and SHRM -SCP®) or other HR-related certifications Special Notes to Applicants The finalist will be subject to a Criminal Background Check and/or a Motor Vehicle Report The Search Committee will not contact references without first verifying permission with the finalist. Please ensure your resume reflects the knowledge, skills, abilities, and experiences to support your answers to the supplemental questions. UNC Charlotte Benefits Information: https://hr.charlotte.edu/benefits/benefits overview/ If there is a document you feel is relevant to this position that you would like reviewed with your resume and application, you may upload it to the “Other Documents” section of the Applicant Documents. Telework Schedule: This position is eligible for a hybrid work arrangement based on successful performance, conduct, completion of required training, and operational needs. After 90 days: Eligibility for up to one (1) remote workday per week . After six months: Consideration may be given for up to two (2) remote workdays per week , contingent upon successful completion of designated training and demonstrated satisfactory performance and conduct. Telework is not guaranteed and is subject to ongoing review and approval by Human Resources leadership. Telework arrangements may be modified or discontinued based on operational or business needs, performance or conduct considerations, or changes to University telework policies, procedures, and practices. Posting Open Date 09/22/2026 Posting Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Proposed Hire Date 10/15/2026 If time-limited please indicate appointment end date Contact Information Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? UNC Charlotte Website HERC Job Board Inside Higher Education Mitratech Circa (formerly known as Local JobNetwork) Another Website Agency Referral Advertisement/Publication Personal Referral Other Where did you learn about this posting? (Open Ended Question) * Bachelor’s degree in human resources, business, psychology, organizational development, or a related field, and at least two years of progressively responsible experience analyzing, interpreting, applying, communicating, and promoting HR best practices in support of organizational goals and objectives; or an equivalent combination of relevant education, training, and experience. Yes, at least a Bachelor’s degree in human resources, business, psychology, organizational development, or a related field, and at least two years of progressively responsible experience analyzing, interpreting, applying, communicating, and promoting HR b Yes, an Associate's degree in human resources, business, psychology, organizational development, or a related field, and at least four years of progressively responsible experience analyzing, interpreting, applying, communicating, and promoting HR best pr Yes, a High School Diploma/GED and at least six years of progressively responsible experience analyzing, interpreting, applying, communicating, and promoting HR best practices in support of organizational goals and objectives. No Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume / Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Contact Information for References Optional Documents Unofficial Transcripts Other Document Writing Sample Other Document 2 Other Document - URL Other Document 3 9201 University City Blvd \r\nCharlotte, NC 28223 © 2026 The University of North Carolina at Charlotte. All rights reserved. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
