    "https://jobs.charlotte.edu/postings/70589": {
      "title": "Position Information",
      "description": "UNC Charlotte Applicant Site | IT Manager II Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Frequently Asked Questions Application Process State of NC Salary Chart Campus Security Report Student Employment IT Manager II Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. The finalist will be subject to a Criminal Background Check and/or a Motor Vehicle Report The Search Committee will not contact references without first verifying permission with the finalist . Please ensure your resume reflects the knowledge, skills, abilities, and experiences to support your answers to the supplemental questions. UNC Charlotte Benefits Information: https://hr.charlotte.edu/benefits/benefits-overview/ Position Information General Information Position Number 008103 Vacancy Open to All Candidates Working Title IT Manager II Position Designation EHRA Non-Faculty Employment Type Permanent - Full-time Months per Year 12 Work Schedule 8:00 am – 5:00 pm; Monday – Friday with occasional evening and weekend hours required, as necessary. Hours per week 40 FLSA Status Exempt Division OneIT Department Office of OneIT (Adm) Work Location Kennedy Salary Range Primary Purpose of Department The Office of OneIT provides highly reliable information technology infrastructure, tools, and services to empower the University to achieve its academic, research, administrative, and service goals. Primary Purpose of Position This position provides leadership and strategic direction for the Data Integrations team, overseeing the design, development, and maintenance of enterprise-level system integrations and APIs. The position ensures reliable, secure, and scalable data exchange between campus ERP , CRM , and third-party systems, while fostering a culture of code standardization and process optimization to support the University’s administrative and academic goals. Summary of Position Responsibilities Lead and mentor a team of integration developers, overseeing professional development, performance management, and daily operational tasks. Design, architect, and manage the lifecycle of enterprise-level system integrations and APIs, ensuring high performance, security, and scalability. Drive the adoption of integration best practices, including API -led connectivity, code standardization, and robust documentation standards across the team. Partner with campus stakeholders to translate complex business requirements into sustainable, automated technical solutions that support academic and administrative goals. Oversee change management, version control, and automated testing strategies to ensure the reliability and security of integration environments. Manage the integration landscape across diverse systems, including ERPs, CRMs, and document management platforms, ensuring seamless data exchange and interoperability. Proactively plan for technology upgrades, capacity management, and infrastructure maintenance to support long-term enterprise scalability. Minimum Education/Experience Bachelor’s degree and 4+ years of relevant work experience. Preferred Education, Knowledge, Skills and Experience Advanced degree in Information Technology, Management Information Systems, or a related field. 5+ years of progressively responsible experience in integration architecture, software development, or IT management. Proven expertise with MuleSoft Anypoint Platform or equivalent iPaaS solutions, including API -led connectivity and API lifecycle management. Strong background in enterprise ERP and CRM systems (e.g., Ellucian Banner, Salesforce). Proficiency in database architecture (Oracle PL/ SQL , SQL ), API modeling languages ( RAML , OpenAPI, Swagger), and Linux environments. Familiarity with DevOps tools and practices (Git, Maven, Jenkins, automated testing, and CI/CD pipelines). Demonstrated experience in leadership, team building, and professional development of technical staff. Excellent communication skills with the ability to manage cross-departmental relationships and translate business requirements into technical solutions. Necessary Certifications/Licenses Preferred Certifications/Licenses Special Notes to Applicants The finalist will be subject to a Criminal Background Check and/or a Motor Vehicle Report The Search Committee will not contact references without first verifying permission with the finalist . Please ensure your resume reflects the knowledge, skills, abilities, and experiences to support your answers to the supplemental questions. UNC Charlotte Benefits Information: https://hr.charlotte.edu/benefits/benefits-overview/ Posting Open Date 09/18/2026 Posting Close Date 10/11/2026 Open Until Filled No Proposed Hire Date If time-limited please indicate appointment end date Contact Information Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? UNC Charlotte Website HERC Job Board Inside Higher Education Mitratech Circa (formerly known as Local JobNetwork) Another Website Agency Referral Advertisement/Publication Personal Referral Other Where did you learn about this posting? (Open Ended Question) * Do you have a Bachelor's degree and four (4)+ years of relevant work experience? Yes, I have a Bachelor's degree and four (4)+ years of relevant work experience No, I do not a Bachelor's degree and four (4)+ years of relevant work experience * Do you live within 100 miles of UNC Charlotte? If not are you willing to relocate for the start of the position? (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume / Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Optional Documents Other Document 9201 University City Blvd \r\nCharlotte, NC 28223 © 2026 The University of North Carolina at Charlotte. All rights reserved. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
