    "https://jobs.charlotte.edu/postings/70637": {
      "title": "Position Information",
      "description": "UNC Charlotte Applicant Site | Admissions Systems Analyst Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Frequently Asked Questions Application Process State of NC Salary Chart Campus Security Report Student Employment Admissions Systems Analyst Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. The finalist will be subject to a Criminal Background Check and/or a Motor Vehicle Report. The Search Committee will not contact references without first verifying permission with the finalist. Please ensure your resume reflects the knowledge, skills, abilities, and experiences to support your answers to the supplemental questions. UNC Charlotte Benefits Information: https://hr.charlotte.edu/benefits/benefits-overview/ Position Information General Information Position Number 000714 Vacancy Open to All Candidates Working Title Admissions Systems Analyst Position Designation EHRA Non-Faculty Employment Type Permanent - Full-time Months per Year 12 Work Schedule Monday – Friday, 8:00 am – 5:00 pm. Nights and weekends are required occasionally. Hours per week 40 FLSA Status Exempt Division Academic Affairs Department Enrollment Management (Adm) Work Location Gage Undergraduate Admissions Center Salary Range $55,000 - $60,000 Primary Purpose of Department The mission of the Undergraduate Admissions Office is to meet the established University enrollment goals by recruiting undergraduate applicants. Our goal is to recruit applicants who can contribute to and profit from the University in academic programs and activities; assist prospects and applicants in realizing their academic ambitions through counseling; accurately and efficiently review academic credentials and notify applicants of decisions; and provide the University community with data necessary for advising and enrollment planning. Our mission statement is “to provide quality service, promote quality service, promote educational opportunities and facilitate enrollment at the University”. We value our position as the first contact a prospective student or the general public may have with the University. Providing timely and accurate information and effectively monitoring the admissions process is critical to the successful recruitment of qualified students. Functionally, the office staff works closely with the faculty and support units on campus and with high school counselors, parents, and community college counselors off-campus. Primary Purpose of Position The Admissions Systems Analyst serves as a key operational and technical liaison within the Office of Undergraduate Admissions, supporting the analysis, improvement, and implementation of admissions-related business processes and systems. This position works closely with Admissions Operations staff, Enrollment Management leadership, and Information Technology partners to identify operational needs, evaluate system functionality, and recommend solutions that improve efficiency, service delivery, and workflow effectiveness. The Admissions Systems Analyst functions as a bridge between business users and technical teams by documenting business requirements, coordinating testing activities, supporting operational projects, and assisting with system enhancements. This role does not perform software development or manage technical data integrations, but instead partners with central IT and vendors to support operational alignment and implementation of approved solutions. Summary of Position Responsibilities Analyze operational challenges and recommend practical solutions consistent with departmental priorities and resources. Analyze admissions workflows to identify process gaps and recommend efficiency improvements. Serve as the primary liaison between the Office of Undergraduate Admissions and campus Information Technology teams regarding operational systems needs and enhancements. Coordinate testing and system validation for upgrades or feature rollouts. Facilitate collaboration among departments, project teams, and campus partners. Develop user guides, SOPs, and training materials; provide direct workflow and system support to internal admissions staff. Create and maintain dashboards/queries, track workflow trends, and support data integrity. Participate effectively as a member of a project team and coordinate assigned project tasks. Other Information about this role: Standard office environment with extended periods of computer use. Occasional evening or weekend work during peak admissions cycles or major operational initiatives. Hybrid work eligibility may be available based on departmental needs and university policy. Minimum Education/Experience Bachelor’s degree from an accredited institution in Business Administration, Information Systems, Higher Education, Public Administration, or a related field. Preferred Education, Knowledge, Skills and Experience Experience working in higher education admissions, enrollment management, or student services operations. Two years of professional experience related to business systems analysis, operations management, project coordination, or process improvement; or an equivalent combination of education and experience. Experience working with student information systems or CRM platforms such as Slate, Banner, PeopleSoft, or Salesforce, with experience analyzing business processes and documenting operational requirements. Experience serving as a liaison between operational units and technical teams, managing priorities while collaborating across departments. Familiarity with project management methodologies, systems testing, and workflow documentation. Knowledge of FERPA and higher education operational compliance standards. Necessary Certifications/Licenses Preferred Certifications/Licenses Special Notes to Applicants The finalist will be subject to a Criminal Background Check and/or a Motor Vehicle Report. The Search Committee will not contact references without first verifying permission with the finalist. Please ensure your resume reflects the knowledge, skills, abilities, and experiences to support your answers to the supplemental questions. UNC Charlotte Benefits Information: https://hr.charlotte.edu/benefits/benefits-overview/ Posting Open Date 09/21/2026 Posting Close Date 10/05/2026 Open Until Filled No Proposed Hire Date 10/26/2026 If time-limited please indicate appointment end date Contact Information Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? UNC Charlotte Website HERC Job Board Inside Higher Education Mitratech Circa (formerly known as Local JobNetwork) Another Website Agency Referral Advertisement/Publication Personal Referral Other Where did you learn about this posting? (Open Ended Question) * Do you have a bachelor’s degree from an accredited institution in Business Administration, Information Systems, Higher Education, Public Administration, or a related field? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume / Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Contact Information for References Optional Documents 9201 University City Blvd \r\nCharlotte, NC 28223 © 2026 The University of North Carolina at Charlotte. All rights reserved. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
